{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council","id":1548164,"title":"Running the Free States - 1 - the Anarch Council","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-03T17:26:53-08:00","id":1548164,"title":"Running the Free States - 1 - the Anarch Council","content":"I will likely run a chronicle set in the Anarch Free States starting in the next few months. I\u2019ll be using some of the ideas I and other players discussed on some other threads on this forum. However, as I'm putting together my notes, I've realized there are a lot of practical considerations that aren't addressed, and I need to figure them out. So I thought to share my ideas here and get other people's feedback, ideas, and commenary.<br /> <br /> Rather than post everything on one big thread that gets clogged up, I\u2019m posting them as separate threads so each subject can get discussed on its own. I\u2019ll add links to the other posts here as edits though, so people can access all threads on this topic.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> <br /> There is an Anarch Council, but that Council does not govern the Free States. Instead it coordinates and supports the Anarchs outside the Free States. The Anarch Council itself is a seven person council that oversees the revolution outside of the Free States. I guess it is something like an Anarch Comintern. This is just one of many things neglected in the Los Angeles By Night sourcebook. While it does not govern the Free States, I imagine internal politics does govern its decisions in some capacity. And it can be an easy source of plot hooks and intrigues for PCs. So I want to figure out what to do with it.<br /> <br /> It is headed by Jeremy MacNeil himself, three other Brujah, and a representative each of the Gangrel, Nosferatu, and Ravnos clans per the Brujah Clanbook 1e.<br /> <br /> The three other Brujah are the Anarch leaders of San Diego, Sacramento, and Seattle. If we accept that as true, we can figure out who they are. Tara is the obvious person to be from San Diego. Later in the Brujah Clanbook, we\u2019re told Marguerite Foccart dwells in Sacramento. She\u2019s a perfect person to be on the Council. That only leaves Seattle, a domain we know little about other than that Justicar Petrodon is stationed there.<br /> <br /> Dark Alliance: Vancouver seems to be the most we have, and all it says is Anarchs have a very hard time in Seattle as Petrodon\u2019s Archons are adept at rooting out and destroying them. Therefore, I will arbitrarily assign Salvador Garcia to this role. First, because I think the author of the Anarch Manifesto and Status Perfectus should be on the Council. Second, he is obviously engaged in supporting the Anarchs outside the city. Third, I will interpret the statement that Garcia is the \u201cleader\u201d of the Seattle Anarchs to be a purposeful tweak at Petrodon as the two vampires are rivals and are in indirect communication with each other.<br /> <br /> = = = =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  adding links 08-01-2025, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T17:40:37-08:00","id":1548167,"title":"","content":"I am reluctantly putting in Ireena from LABN as the Ravnos representative. I say reluctantly because her biography in LABN is not very impressive. The Council does not really gain anything by her presence. She\u2019s very young, only tenth generation, and not really leading anyone. She doesn\u2019t bring anything to the table.<br /> <br /> However, she was part of the group that attacked Don Sebastian\u2019s ranch, and identified the havens of the elders of LA so the anarchs could attack them. She wanders the Free States and the Pacific Northwest, doing what she can to damage the Camarilla. She helps anarchs wherever she can, and fights the Camarilla and Sabbat. I am forced to admit she is the most likely candidate. She actually has no political influence among other vampires. She seems to just do her own thing although her presence probably brings some sympathy and occasional support from other Ravnos.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s probably not going to argue much with the Brujah on the Council. She either misses any votes or debates entirely, or likely agrees with whatever was decided. She\u2019s a reliable partner to MacNeil, Foccart, and Garcia, and that is probably the only thing that matters. She\u2019s figleaf to show the Anarchs as being more representative than what they really are.<br /> <br /> As such, I imagine PCs will likely assume she is of much more importance than what she really is. She's also a way to introduce the idea of other Ravnos dwelling in the Fee States or visiting there without the harassment and problems that are encountered in more traditional domains. It could also be a complication for Gangrel in the Free States as their rivalry with that clan is not part of Camarilla dynamics. And many Barons aren't going to welcome them any more than Camarilla Princes would. I also think it is possible to show that the Ravnos are their own thing, and aren't actually anarchs. The clan may be very loosely organized and its members have a lot of freedom, but Ravnos neonates aren't at war with their elders in the same way the anarchs are at war. Ravnos elders are different from the elders of other clans, but they are still elders. This clan has different goals and ideas than the anarchs even if there are some common interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T17:46:01-08:00","id":1548169,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think there are any known likely candidates for the Gangrel and Nosferatu candidates on the Council. LABN does not mention any Gangrel at all, and it\u2019s single mention of a Nosferatu is one that remains hidden and isn\u2019t devoted to the anarchs. Nor do I remember any canonical characters from the clanbooks or elsewhere that would be a good fit. We do get mentions of occasional anarchs among these clans, but nobody of importance.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ll need to make my own. I am thinking of making one a \u201ctraditional\u201d Anarch associated with egalitarian issues as a mortal, I am also thinking the other should be someone who as a mortal would be seen on the \u201cwrong\u201d side, but was unfortuately embraced with a weak generation and thus denied a chance for real power in the Camarilla. Similar to the rich yuppie Gordon Keaton in Chicago By Night who was a Caitiff or if Hortatio Ballard was only 12<sup>th</sup> generation. Someone very capable who would have been part of the Camarilla power structure except for those aspects that disenfranchised her. The former will probably be the Gangrel and the latter the Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> However, if people have any candidates from canon, or just ideas on interesting templates or concepts for it, I\u2019d love to hear them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T15:38:06-08:00","id":1548209,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like Tyrus and the Wolf Pack from Chicago by Night but Anarchs. If they control an MC, they can use that as cover to move all kinds of supplies across the country to Anarch Cells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T05:10:43-08:00","id":1548250,"title":"","content":"Given the nature of the Anarch Free States as a place where the Revolution came, The Man went down and quite a lot of the Revolutionaries promptly cried \u201cJob done, PARTY TIME!\u201d whilst others hollered \u201cKATANAS! KATANAS! KATANAS!\u201d and the most important single grown-up was so determined not to become a tyrant that he decided to play Cincinattus when it was really, really time to play George Washington, I\u2019d argue that it makes perfect sense for the Anarch Council to be at least a little bit more of a talking shop with enormous potential for either rationalising the Free States Revolution (and taking this show on the road) or falling prey to the \u2018tall poppy\u2019 syndrome so inherent to those who have overthrown their \u2018elders &amp; betters\u2019 and are fully prepared to spend the foreseeable future tearing down anyone (or any group) who starts looking a little <i>too</i> much like the Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Anarch Council has to walk a fine line between exerting it\u2019s influence and avoiding being see as The Authorities if it wants to avoid becoming a might-have-been (Like the Kerensky-led version of Russia): with that in mind, it makes perfect sense that it\u2019s members would have to eat a certain amount of humble pie, whilst also keeping a weather eye out for the Camarilla answer to the Freikorps, the Free State\u2019s equivalent to Lenin &amp; the Bolsheviks, as well as the fear of next year\u2019s Stalin emerging from their own ranks.<br /> <br /> Basically, it\u2019s easy to imagine the Council\u2019s members as an interesting mix of True Believers seeking to spread The Revolution, pragmatists attempting to fit a safety valve to the Katanas-Trenchcoats-Nineties Action Movie mayhem of the Free States (Presumably by throwing some of the louder enthusiasts against Camarilla strongholds or Sabbat forward bases), Exiles looking to drum up support for their own comeback tour, cynics looking to profit off The Revolution (Of only by building their own reputation in Anarch circles) and perhaps the tidy-minded, looking to impose some actual structure on vampires of the \u2018Wild, Wild West Coast\u2019 (Especially in it\u2019s beating heart, before everybody suffers a heart attack and/or BUFFY THE VAMPIRE SLAYER becomes a chillingly accurate documentary).<br /> <br /> <br /> Put another way, I\u2019d argue that Ireena of Clan Ravnos makes a perfect member of the Anarch Free States - especially as the \u2018Face\u2019 of the Council - as she\u2019s active, idealistic and takes the lead without being someone the Anarchs will look at and see as a potential threat to their freedom to do whatever the **** they feel like (Much less somebody who has \u2018Future Prince of LA\u2019 hanging over them like a gathering storm), not least due to her own fairly puny generation.<br /> <br /> All of which means she has relatively little muscle of her own, but is also a \u2018tabula rasa\u2019 more likely to be judged on her (Impeccably Anarch) actions than on any past history.<br /> <br /> <br /> The real problem, of course, is coming up with other members for the Anarch Council who have enough age and blood potency to be useful, but come<br /> across as enough of a clean slate (or possess sufficient local goodwill) to avoid contracting a dangerous case of Tall Poppy Syndrome.<br /> <br /> Well, that and ensuring that members build up the Free States as a whole without conjuring up a personal base of support so potent they pull a \u2018crown from the gutter\u2019 move, <i>a la</i> Napoleon.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m assuming that, whether as associates of the Anarch Council or as agents thereof, it\u2019s the Player Characters who will/would have played the key role in making the Free States and their Revolution work, with the canonical fate of LA serving as a prime example of what happens when they adventure off on a frolic of their own instead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T05:27:53-08:00","id":1548251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548169#post1548169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think there are any known likely candidates for the Gangrel and Nosferatu candidates on the Council. LABN does not mention any Gangrel at all, and it\u2019s single mention of a Nosferatu is one that remains hidden and isn\u2019t devoted to the anarchs. Nor do I remember any canonical characters from the clanbooks or elsewhere that would be a good fit. We do get mentions of occasional anarchs among these clans, but nobody of importance.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ll need to make my own. I am thinking of making one a \u201ctraditional\u201d Anarch associated with egalitarian issues as a mortal, I am also thinking the other should be someone who as a mortal would be seen on the \u201cwrong\u201d side, but was unfortuately embraced with a weak generation and thus denied a chance for real power in the Camarilla. Similar to the rich yuppie Gordon Keaton in Chicago By Night who was a Caitiff or if Hortatio Ballard was only 12<sup>th</sup> generation. Someone very capable who would have been part of the Camarilla power structure except for those aspects that disenfranchised her. The former will probably be the Gangrel and the latter the Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> However, if people have any candidates from canon, or just ideas on interesting templates or concepts for it, I\u2019d love to hear them.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> , I took one look at this and my imagination screamed \u201cCHALLENGE ACCEPTED!\u201d, with the result that I have a number of character concepts to share: fair warning, I\u2019m acquainted with the general situation in LA BY NIGHT and have a vague acquaintance with some of the LA players in BLOODLINES, but haven\u2019t really researched these subjects in a year of more (Also, I\u2019m mostly limited to freely-available online sources), so most of what follows is fairly archetypical \u2018California Vampires\u2019 stuff rather than tailor-made.<br /> <br /> Also, you might notice a certain fondness on my<br /> part for embracing the Larger than Life: I make no apologies.<br /> <br /> <br /> THE DARK HIDALGO (aka Vampire Zorro): A gentleman and the son of a gentleman from Old California who found himself getting caught up in the Wars of Independence elsewhere in Spanish America on his way back from an education in the Old Country (In highly dashing style) and only reached California after being made a vampire.<br /> <br /> Promptly decided that he preferred not to live upon the blood of his own people, he devoted himself to continuing the struggle for freedom a safe distance from his homeland, continuing to pay the occasional visit to his old hacienda \u2026 right up until they built modern Los Angeles all over the place and proceeded to make life more difficult for Hispanic Americans (Not least because he had far less compunction about living off the tidal wave of strangers who swept into the LA area in their masses).<br /> <br /> At which point, of course, the old cape came out of the cupboard: to say that this fine fellow was less than popular with the Camarilla establishment would be an understatement, but nothing had been proven before the Anarch Revolt came and gave Our Hero a new lease on life.<br /> <br /> Now the only problem is that he\u2019s too posh to be entirely trusted. too idealistic to keep quiet and too old in the blood to be safely ignored.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Please note that this concept is, alas, not Clan Specific: on the other hand it\u2019s quite amusing and so I produced it first.<br /> <br /> More to come.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T05:56:09-08:00","id":1548252,"title":"","content":"Right, now we get to the Clan Specific bits (The following are all from Clan Gangrel):-<br /> <br /> <br /> AVENGING INTERNEE - A Japanese American girl who had an experience of the Second World War that, coupled with life as a budding 1950s housewife, left her with such a burden of quiet anger that a passing Gangrel noticed and gave her the chance to let that anger Roar. <br /> <br /> Embracing her wild side, though more interested in clawing out territory in the Urban Jungle, she came to Los Angeles and very quickly learned that the vampire authorities were no more loveable than the All-American establishment : to say she embraced the Anarch Revolution is rather like saying a starving mother embraces the prospect of a steak dinner \u2026 <br /> <br /> <br /> COUNTER-CULTURE REVOLUTIONARY (aka \u2018Feral Hippy\u2019): Was keen to become one with nature even before that Gangrel rose from the Earth the way a dolphin leaps from the sea and rejoiced in their new animal vigour after somehow convincing a Gangrel to make them a vampire (Possibly even the same one, though our hero remains somewhat unclear on that particular point).<br /> <br /> It seems highly likely they did so by demonstrating a willingness to do whatever it took just short of making themselves as enough of a Yes Man to be marked down for perpetual ghoul-dom, then proceeded to build a career as a surprisingly-groovy Feral (Not least as something of an ambassador between other Gangrel and the local vampires).<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly became caught up in the undercurrent of pure loathing towards the LA Camarilla (and towards the Camarilla as a whole) this particular specimen became outright carried away with enthusiasm for the Anarch Rebellion and the Free States, but (to the surprise of many) has turned out to be enough of a Bug Picture thinker to start advocating that the Anarchs take their show on the road, inevitably bringing him into the orbit of the Anarch Council.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>It now occurs to me that the logical way of making this sometime Hippy a logical fit for the Anarch Council would be to show him having some history as a smuggler, with at least some history of running drugs &amp; guns, as well as general smuggling (Not least of ideas).</i><br /> <br /> <br /> THE SPIRIT OF 1976 - A Native American Rights advocate of somewhat violent temper who caught the attention of an elder Gangrel and was, in part through sheer disillusion, won over to the idea of becoming a vampire.<br /> <br /> Arriving in Camarilla society with the mixture of American Pride, disillusion, outrage and pure cynicism towards Authority so peculiar to the 1970s, he swiftly learned to love Vampire Society just as much as he loved the US authorities. <br /> <br /> Having been a budding Anarch ever since their days as a fledgling, they are finally beginning to bloom into the Revolutionary they had dreamed of becoming, though whether this will be a cure or a vehicle for their persistent cynicism is an interesting question \u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T06:33:40-08:00","id":1548253,"title":"","content":"Now for Clan Nosferatu (One or two sensible notions and one crackpot theory):-<br /> <br /> BEAR STATE REVOLUTIONARY (Deformity: looks like somebody shaved a man-sized bear and dressed it like people not long before it developed a hellish case of five o\u2019clock shadow): An Anglo who arrived early in California and participated with great enthusiasm in the Bear Flag Revolt,<br /> memories of victory in that particular effort proved of great comfort when Our Hero was \u2018acquired\u2019 by Clan Nosferatu on their arrival in California (One member having a notion to acquire intelligence on the varying deposits of the \u201849 Gold Rush so they they could parley it to any other licks that showed up with an eye to hostile takeovers).<br /> <br /> Having been promptly retained as a local guide and becoming the Clan\u2019s very own Mountain Man in California and the Mountain West, this particular Kindred found his particular set of skills increasingly surplus to requirements as California grew more tame (Except when it came to scouting out Lupines), became lonely for Kindred company (Not least because dodging Lupines is an interesting hobby but a terrifying night job) and finally grew nostalgic enough for his days as a Rebel to add his voice to the Anarch roar.<br /> <br /> Now if only they\u2019d let him running embassies to San Francisco and quit asking what he thinks the **** werewolves are up to. He misses \u2018Frisco, he NEVER misses the **** Lupines.<br /> <br /> <br /> THE PROFESSIONAL (Deformity: He\u2019s all eyes) - Nobody is quite certain how old The Professional is, not least because he\u2019s too old an information-broker to share anything about himself without adequate compensation: what is known is that he\u2019s as fluent in French as he is in Russian and that he\u2019s a Lick who knows how to make a Revolution work and has even been known to work for The Revolution (Some claim he\u2019s most expert in how to make The Revolution work from him, but that may well be slander from rivals and those most concerned that a perfectly useful spymaster is never more than one visit to Hugo Boss away from becoming a Secret Policeman).<br /> <br /> <i>NOTE: At this point it should be noted that I have only just looked up \u2018Los Angeles\u2019 on the White Wolf Wiki and thoroughly<br /> embarrassed myself by seeing that the Anarch Revolt occurred in the 1940s - this will mean, of course, that a number of my character concepts must be revised (Though most of them only in relatively small details, or so I hope).</i> <br /> <br /> <i>In my defence I wanted to get my ideas out before my self-confidence flagged.</i><br /> <br /> Anyway, The Professional is a character who epitomises the sort of orderly, clear-sighted and professional revolutionary who could potentially bring the Free Staters out in droves for what used to be called a \u2018necktie party\u2019 - while he\u2019s most often a hired gun looking to make the local Revolution work, he\u2019s potentially old enough and certainly enigmatic enough to make an excellent candidate for the role of \u2018Next Year\u2019s Stalin (The moustache certainly doesn\u2019t help, though he\u2019s been known to claim it started as a hussar moustache).<br /> <br /> As a result, he tends spend to periods in Los Angeles, followed by periods somewhere else that quietly-but-inevitably acquires an Anarch problem (No matter where that somewhere might actually be).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T06:44:46-08:00","id":1548254,"title":"","content":"Right, those were the sensible - no, wait, I forgot to suggest one sensible notion:<br /> <br /> THE HACK (Deformity:Two-faced) - A Hollywood writer who built his career before and during the Second World War, got caught up in the Red Scare and became a vampire when their sheer disillusion with the Beautiful People became something a Nosferatu could only admire &amp; hope to perpetuate.<br /> <br /> I started this archetype with the idea of the character as scriptwriter who turned snitch during HUAC (Then became deeply disillusioned with Hollywood and their own hypocrisy), but now I\u2019m wondering if they should be a failed scriptwriter turned tabloid hack and HUAC informer (With the latter phase of their career the point at which they lost all love of the Beautiful People and their Dream Factor, the death knell of the ambition and the dream, but not the drive, that had brought them to Hollywood in the first place).<br /> <br /> These days mostly acts as a ghost writer/silent partner for a number of media types, but keeps struggling with the fact that they\u2019re a newspaper writer in an increasingly multimedia world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>NOTE: I\u2019ve mostly been writing these ideas with the notion that they\u2019re for the original, circa 1994 setting of LA BY NIGHT. The key exception is next up, but seems gonzo enough to deserve a separate entry. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T07:02:37-08:00","id":1548256,"title":"","content":"CRACKPOT THEORY TIME - As you might imagine, when writing up ideas for Vampire Los Angeles circa the 1990s, with the benefit of 30 years and some months of hindsight, BUFFY THE VAMPIRE SLAYER came to mind and ANGEL: THE SERIES came calling with a welcome basket, as well as what may or may not have been Menaces touching on the probable consequences of not becoming a key influence on Vampire Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> All of which is a prelude to and an excuse for my latest Crackpot Theory: the most entertaining way to include pastiches of ANGEL and other noteworthy BUFFY-type vampires into the Old World of Darkness would be as member of Clan Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Two Words: GAME FACE.<br /> <br /> On a slightly more serious note, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, you\u2019ve noted before that you\u2019re disappointed that Clan Nosferatu are too often depicted with a culture of slumming it: by taking advantage of the fact that The Master was literally modelled on Graf Orlock (The original NOSFERATU) and that his descendants (As well as all other vampires in the TV series) are depicted with some blatantly monstrous visages* to build pastiches (Presumably affectionate pastiches) of those characters as members of the Clan legendary for producing the stuff of Creature Features by the nature of their Curse, you would swiftly acquire a charismatic selection of Nosferatu with a stereotype-busting range of personalities.<br /> <br /> Also, making the \u2018Order of Aurelius\u2019 Nosferatu would allow you to explore the major differences of tone &amp; style between the Buffy-verse and the World of Darkness (How different would the characters of Angel and Spike be if they could never STOP looking like monsters, for example?).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m running out of time to go into more detail - Battery down to the dregs - but it does strike me that \u2018Damon\u2019 (A Nosferatu who seems to think he\u2019s a born Brujah, with a brutal history and a strong vein of tragic romance who may or may not be one of the more prolific vampire hunters in Los Angeles and is certainly a sometime Vampire PI) might make for an interesting member of the Anarch Council.<br /> <br /> <br /> * (Albeit ones they can put on and out off, probably with an act of deliberate will).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T07:15:08-08:00","id":1548257,"title":"","content":"Also, this is of course a suggestion that there be a running joke about Free State Vampires perpetuating urban legends about a there being a perky blonde cheerleader with keen fashion skills and a body count running longer than the average film franchise somewhere in South California, because SOMEONE keeps picking licks off and it isn\u2019t any of the Usual Suspects and it wasn\u2019t the storyteller either.<br /> <br /> Whether this is purely an urban legends, an ongoing effort to cover up the work of something else or a genuinely-gifted hunter most active between AD 1992 and 1997 (Well the inspiration for the series would have to come from somewhere, In-universe) I leave to the individual storyteller.<br /> <br /> Also, I am inches away from throwing in a part-time Occult Investigator, full-time Lifeguard as an homage to BAYWATCH NIGHTS in particular and the surprising amount of spooky stuff in BAYWATCH as a whole, but I\u2019m not sure my good reputation would survive such an affectionate homage to \u201890s TV trivia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T10:59:22-08:00","id":1548262,"title":"","content":"Zorro is a name I haven't heard in a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T11:47:01-08:00","id":1548264,"title":"","content":"Clearly you haven\u2019t been living in my imagination, where Mr Banderas, Mr Langella and Mr Power (Amongst others) live rent-free.<br /> <br /> Not just because they\u2019re dashing rogues perfectly able to dive out the window either!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T14:00:39-08:00","id":1548265,"title":"","content":"Fantastic work,<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a>!<br /> <br /> I wrote a novel for submission to 5th Edition as a pitch for reviving the book spin offs of VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE last year called KNIGHT OF FREEDOM that was one of two I completed. The project was rejected but the other one would have starred Lucita. Knight of Freedom had the premise that Theo Bell has been hiding in the Anarch Free States for the past decade or so since his assassination of Hardelstadt and kept expecting the hammer to fall down. The joke was that Theo Bell was living a comparative life of luxury being passed around between the Barons and the Camarilla had no real interest in assassinating him for reasons that were revealed in the novel. But also because Theo Bell worked much better as an unliving Non-Red List symbol of Anarch perfidy than someone they wanted to martyr.<br /> <br /> Among the things I established in the book was the following:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Baron Louis Fortier</b>: The ruler of Bel-Air and one of the most powerful Barons around as well as the richest, he's also someone all of the Anarchs are generally embarrassed about. Mostly because he's a Ventrue French potentate who rule exactly like a Prince except perhaps an unusually generous one. Louis is notably someone who is aware of the fact that as ruler of a huge chunk of LA, he's more powerful than most Princes in America and has the mind that if he allied with the Camarilla, they'd swiftly replace him with someone else. Ergo, he's quite happy to be like Napoleon and claim he's all for the Revolution while wielding immense power. All of his wives have left him but he continually ends up finding new young Kindred mistresses since he has a most- Un-Elder obsession with Sex.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The MacNeils</b>: This is not actually a Barony but a Clan of Brujah descended from the Beckoned or dead Jeremy. They constantly feud for power and routinely end up staking each other but never kill one another. The current leader is his youngest progeny who helped steal the Stone of Scone in 1950. Annie MacDougal is a pain in the ass for all Anarchs because she insists anyone not like Jeremy is failing to be Anarch enough. Many think he bloodbound her before he went away because no Kindred could be that stupidly loyal.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Undisputed Baron of the Valley, Victor Temple</b>: Yet another Ventrue who has weasaled his way to the top, he's a lot more accepted by Baron Fortier but only because he's younger and hipper with a reputation roughly akin to Suge Knight's. His affable demeanor conceals as much violence and ruthlessness as any other Ventrue ruler, though. He is also somewhat careless with the Masquerade and this is likely to get him killed well before his other stunts. He recently has begun feuding with longtime ally Nelli-G.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Hesha Ruhadze</b>: The Ministry archaeologist and Theopidian joining with the breakaway sect was something few expected but he's taken over the Church of Set and become heavily involved in counter-culture Satanism as a trick to lure in vessels as well as attack traditional religion. He lives in Pasadena and generally leaves most of the regular Anarch business to lesser childer as he focuses on Clan business. Generally, Hesha's opinion of the Anarchs can be summarized as, &quot;same blood, different vessels.&quot; He is a cynical old snake who thinks there is no difference between the Camarilla and Anarchs than the former smell better but he's dealt with plenty of peasant revolutions and rabble rousers before. It'll all come together eventually around an elite he's already a member of.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Nelli G</b>: The beautiful Toreador descendant of the Griffith family, Nelli G is a habitual traitor to the Kindred race and has allied with the Second Inquisition to eliminate her enemies in Hollywood. She's also surrendered Griffith Park to the Garou, causing a small war with the local Gangrel (led by Ramona). Her humanity has gone down rapidly since the murder of her sire and doesn't seem to be stopping as the power has gotten to her. She is the Lady of Hollywood and its strip, controlling kindred who want fame, money, drugs, and blood. Her second in command is Vivi and she is already plotting against her, which Nelli approves of as it keeps her sharp.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Nines Rodriguez</b>: Nines is pissed and is unlikely to stop being so any time soon. He's been essentially given a role to help protect the Masquerade in the city by all of the Barons allowing him free passage as well as to that of his gang. It's a role that Nines notes is suspiciously similar to that of a Sheriff even though he considers himself a Cleaner. He also feels like some people want him to have even more power that would make him, you guessed it, a Baron of Barons. One, of course, with lots of powerful Barons as a Council behind him. Nines is disgusted and is wondering if they should put Theo in charge just as a F-U to the system. He HATES Hesha.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>Theresa/Jeanette</b>: The very much disputed Baron of Santa Monica and several other territories, Theresa and Jeanette are direly opposed to one another but between them control everything but the Pier. They are surprisingly accepting of Thin Bloods and other immigrants. She's also one of the most ruthless in destroying them or playing them off against her &quot;sister.&quot; Theresa is notable in that she also controls a large chunk of Las Vegas from the Asylum franchise there and is debating giving up one territory for the other. Basically, Sin City is ripe for picking and the Hecata have made her an offer to be their figurehead.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Smiling Jack and Jenna Cross</b>: Smiling Jack was, unsurprisingly, Beckoned given his age and obsession with Noddism. What's weird is he claims he's back from the Middle East and with greater insight than ever. His adopted childe, Jenna Cross, has also become head of one of the largest Duskborn groups in America with over forty members. While based in Santa Monica, they are spread all through California and on the web. It is here they are working on using Thin Blooded Alchemy to try to win a place in the Anarchs equal to a Clan.<br /> <br /> 9. <b>Wei: </b>: An invasion of the Tzimisce from China briefly disrupted the life of many Asian American Kindred in California. Wei was embraced by one of them and helped lead a revolt after their leader was assassinated by the LA Ripper. Wei is now in control of Chinatown and generally has the view that they're Americans and weird clan abilities shouldn't mean much. Still, he's as power hungry and ruthless as any other Kindred leader. Ironically, Wei has a big secret he's keeping from his former Anarchs that will destroy him. The irony is that it's not a typical Kindred secret: it's that he was a former undercover LA detective.<br /> <br /> 10. <b>Ramona</b>:\u200b Ramona is weirded out by the fact that as an anti-social Gangrel who never was close to her clan, she's become a celebrity for her part in the defection to the Anarchs. Ironically, her aloofness means that people take her &quot;fuck off and figure it out for yourself&quot; attitude as wisdom. Reluctantly, she's become a den mother for other Gangrel in the city and many Dustborn and Caitiff. She has also claimed Griffith Park for her territory and the expected massacre by the Garou Nelli G counted on didn't happen. They apparently are having their own issues and the caern there is temporarily abandoned. Ramona rarely spends time there anyway and mostly uses her &quot;dominion&quot; there as a title to scare people away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T14:11:01-08:00","id":1548266,"title":"","content":"Oh and these two:<br /> <br /> 11. <b>The Los Angeles Ripper</b>: A mysterious Kindred embraced during the short-lived reign of Prince La Croix. Not much is known about them, even their clan, though many believe them to be a Malkavian who uses Obfuscate to impersonate other Clans or even genders. The Los Angeles Ripper is believed to have been a very Low Generation Cainite who also had unusual strength for a Neonate and destroyed several Elders despite being only a few weeks old. He/she is considered something of an unofficial Scourge, working against troublemakers. Ironically, they're well-liked among the Dustborn and believed to be involved somehow with Jenna Cross. They are also partial to redheads.<br /> <br /> 12. <b>Vannevar Thomas: </b> The third Prince of LA, he's actually close to being the Prince of Glendale. Ironically, that's actually better than most princes and since recovering his sanity after being tortured by Theresa/Jeanette, he's become somewhat tolerated among the Anarchs. Vannevar is aware that he was sent to LA to die and is now plotting his own long-term strategy: to regain San Fransisco. While few Anarchs would willingly ally with Cammie scum, he's very persuasive and very rich. As such, he's gradually built up a cadre of allies. Ironically, his brief insanity also seems to have knocked the Beckoning from his system and he notes he has outlived a lot of his former enemies. He is accompanied by his consort, Susan, who is as typical a Toreador as exists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T16:32:20-08:00","id":1548273,"title":"","content":"It's nice to see Ramona Tanner-Childe getting some exposure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T17:09:44-08:00","id":1548280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548250#post1548250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, the Anarch Council has to walk a fine line between exerting it\u2019s influence and avoiding being see as The Authorities if i</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarch Council does not run the Free States. It is not mentioned at all in LABN. There the sourcebook describes how the city is actually &quot;governed&quot;. A future thread will talk about the practicalities of governance. The purpose of the Anarch Council instead is to assist anarchs <i>elsewhere</i> in their fight. It's one reason why many of the anarchs on the Council don't actually live in Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> So the Kindred of Los Angeles don't really pay the Anarch Council any heed because it isn't their governance. It also is not responsible for the defense of the Free States. Although I assume some of the local anarchs do indeed volunteer their services to help the cause. Certainly both Salvador Garcia and Crispus Attucks are often absent from the city for that reason. I assume Smiling Jack also agrees to take on odd task as he travels frequently. And I assume roving nomadic coteries like &quot;Carlyle's Gang&quot; from Chicago By Night, 2e serves the Council, but often come back to Los Angeles for rest and relaxation. Of course, all of this is on a volunteer basis only. They aren't soldiers who have to obey orders, so they are just very motivated.<br /> <br /> The primary importance of the Council is to anarchs in other cities who know they have someone trying to help them to some degree.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T12:35:06-08:00","id":1548302,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, in all humility I would like to point to my not having brushed up on LOS ANGELES BY NIGHT before posting my ideas (For fear of smothering my self-confidence with too many details), hence any number of misconceptions in my posts above.<br /> <br /> Mea culpa, mea culpa, mea maxima culpa.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, thank you for the kind words and my compliments on your own fine additions to the thread.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (It amuses me to imagine the MacNeils pigheadedly going around calling themselves \u2018The MacNeil Clan\u2019 - not \u2018Clan MacNeil\u2019 for obvious reasons - and referring to the lamented Jeremy MacNeil as \u2018The MacNeil\u2019, despite almost none of them being actual Scots and absolutely none of them being from the Highlands and Islands).<br /> <br /> <br /> It also interests me to speculate on what the former Prince<br /> of San Francisco thinks of his Ventrue neighbours: I suspect that Clan ties would have been kept up as a channel of unofficial communications between the Free States and their quietest neighbour, but that doesn\u2019t mean they actually like each other.<br /> <br /> Also, given Old Thomas\u2019 love of sea life, I wonder if he\u2019s<br /> settle somewhere close to the ocean, while in Los Angeles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T12:37:01-08:00","id":1548303,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s a thought: I wonder if it was Vannevar Thomas\u2019 history as a soldier in the American War of Independence that helped keep open war with the Anarchs from breaking out in San Francisco? (Here\u2019s an interesting thought: how different might history have been had Jeremy MacNeil decided on San Francisco, not Los Angeles as his new home?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T18:28:52-08:00","id":1548316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548303#post1548303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here\u2019s a thought: I wonder if it was Vannevar Thomas\u2019 history as a soldier in the American War of Independence that helped keep open war with the Anarchs from breaking out in San Francisco? (Here\u2019s an interesting thought: how different might history have been had Jeremy MacNeil decided on San Francisco, not Los Angeles as his new home?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a future thread planned about San Francisco and its relation to the Free States. I will be setting the chronicle in the early nineties and utilizing a lot of early edition material as inspiration. I say inspiration because lots of canon is terrible so I am only using the things I like or can turn into things I like.<br /> <br /> San Francisco never got its own city book despite a lot of things being established about it. A lot of early WoD fiction was set place in San Francisco, so we do get a lot of information if you bother to read these novels and short stories. More importantly we get a write up of &quot;the Vampire Club&quot; in A World of Darkness, 1e. Despite San Francisco being Camarilla, it is intended as a kind of &quot;Casablanca&quot; where all kinds of vampires can meet and intrigue with the Vampire Club being analogous to Rick's Cafe Americain. Very unusually, it mentions that it was the site of the 1946 Conclave that resulted in the \u201cPalatine Treaty\u201d which gave the domain of San Francisco almost unheard of autonomy. The domain of San Francisco was called the Palatinate of San Francisco, and its Primogen the Palatine Council.<br /> <br /> In historical terms, &quot;palatines&quot; were usually lower lords who nevertheless assumed some of the functions that normally the crown itself would have. In this case, presumably the Prince of San Francisco might be invested with powers normally delegated to the Justicars. Whether that is actually the case is unknown.<br /> <br /> It's not clear to me what exactly that may mean, but I am leaning to the idea that the Justicars and Archons leave it alone even though the domain is governed by Camarilla standards. Presumably there are a lot more details in the &quot;Treaty&quot; that would proscribe when the Justicars might intervene. Presumably this is to justify its status as &quot;Casablanca&quot; in its &quot;Vichy, but Neutral&quot; role. Prince Vannevar Thomas himself is probably more of a Major Strasser type with Sebastian Melmoth more like Captain Renault and Tex R Cainan as Rick Blaine.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs do seem to view San Francisco and Prince Vannevar Thomas as a threat, but presumably its nebulous status suits both the Anarchs and Justicar Petrodon.<br /> <br /> I do want to have San Francisco be an active element in my Free States chronicle and trying to figure out how to integrate that and the Vampire Club, but it's such a big enough topic I'm reserving it for its own thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-08T06:18:25-08:00","id":1548323,"title":"","content":"Well it did get this.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/538/san-francisco-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/prod...cisco-by-night</a><br /> <br /> It was not a great supplement since it portrayed the Yellow Peril to a full 1000% and ignored Vannevar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-08T10:26:06-08:00","id":1548325,"title":"","content":"From what I read on the link, it wasn't very popular with fans of Vampire The Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-08T23:35:29-08:00","id":1548329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548325#post1548325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I read on the link, it wasn't very popular with fans of Vampire The Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>It basically seemed to be written by someone who had no idea who Vannevar Thomas was or any of the San Fransisco info that previously existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-08T23:36:29-08:00","id":1548330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548273#post1548273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nice to see Ramona Tanner-Childe getting some exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've used her in my games since then and there's an interesting idea that in the 5th Edition era, a vampire who has survived for twenty years or so is almost an elder to Anarchs due to the massive deaths and purges.<br /> <br /> (Which I use to explain why Neonates seem so aggressively ignorant in the modern era)<br /> <br /> It's a role she's deeply annoyed by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T10:23:30-08:00","id":1548337,"title":"","content":"Now all that is needed is having Hesha's Childe to make an appearance in your game and see how she will react that her sure is involved with the Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T10:02:30-08:00","id":1548368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548316#post1548316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a future thread planned about San Francisco and its relation to the Free States. I will be setting the chronicle in the early nineties and utilizing a lot of early edition material as inspiration. I say inspiration because lots of canon is terrible so I am only using the things I like or can turn into things I like.<br /> <br /> San Francisco never got its own city book despite a lot of things being established about it. A lot of early WoD fiction was set place in San Francisco, so we do get a lot of information if you bother to read these novels and short stories. More importantly we get a write up of &quot;the Vampire Club&quot; in A World of Darkness, 1e. Despite San Francisco being Camarilla, it is intended as a kind of &quot;Casablanca&quot; where all kinds of vampires can meet and intrigue with the Vampire Club being analogous to Rick's Cafe Americain. Very unusually, it mentions that it was the site of the 1946 Conclave that resulted in the \u201cPalatine Treaty\u201d which gave the domain of San Francisco almost unheard of autonomy. The domain of San Francisco was called the Palatinate of San Francisco, and its Primogen the Palatine Council.<br /> <br /> In historical terms, &quot;palatines&quot; were usually lower lords who nevertheless assumed some of the functions that normally the crown itself would have. In this case, presumably the Prince of San Francisco might be invested with powers normally delegated to the Justicars. Whether that is actually the case is unknown.<br /> <br /> It's not clear to me what exactly that may mean, but I am leaning to the idea that the Justicars and Archons leave it alone even though the domain is governed by Camarilla standards. Presumably there are a lot more details in the &quot;Treaty&quot; that would proscribe when the Justicars might intervene. Presumably this is to justify its status as &quot;Casablanca&quot; in its &quot;Vichy, but Neutral&quot; role. Prince Vannevar Thomas himself is probably more of a Major Strasser type with Sebastian Melmoth more like Captain Renault and Tex R Cainan as Rick Blaine.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs do seem to view San Francisco and Prince Vannevar Thomas as a threat, but presumably its nebulous status suits both the Anarchs and Justicar Petrodon.<br /> <br /> I do want to have San Francisco be an active element in my Free States chronicle and trying to figure out how to integrate that and the Vampire Club, but it's such a big enough topic I'm reserving it for its own thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now this sounds like another fine thread to be forthcoming!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming that the \u2018Casablanca\u2019 analogy is one usually floated by the Anarchs (With Camarilla sorts, especially in the AD 1990s, preferring to evoke West Berlin - as an island of the Good Life amidst a tide of Revolutionary Brutality and an outpost in the very mouth of the lion).<br /> <br /> One would, additionally, be prepared to hazard a guess that San Francisco might have been deliberately preserved by the Free Staters as a \u2018hostage to fortune\u2019 (allowed to continue existing as much because being able to threaten an isolated Camarilla city, if only implicitly, added to the bargaining power of the Anarch Movement) - though it\u2019s also possible the city acted as a safety valve, allowing those who wanted to quit the Free States to do so without actually escaping them, per se.<br /> <br /> - Incidentally, I wonder if the presence of an active and powerful Caern in the region (with ties to no fewer than two Trobes) might have made the Free States more reluctant to push their luck in the Golden Bay? (The Free States expect to see combat, but picking a fight with the OG Combat Monsters of the World of Darkness is something even Njnes Rodriguez probably doesn\u2019t do by choice).<br /> <br /> - One also wonders if there might be some way to smuggle elements from KINDRED: THE EMBRACED into your version of \u2018Bay City\u2019? (I\u2019ve amused myself once or twice by wondering if Julian Luna and Vannevar Thomas might have been considered for the role of Prince at much the same<br /> time and arrived at a \u2018gentleman\u2019s agreement\u2019 not to meddle should the other have received the honour*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *In fact, I\u2019ve gone so far as to wonder if making fellow \u2018Reasonable Ventrue\u2019 Vannevar Thomas\u2019 preferred successor at his \u2018abdication\u2019 would lend an interesting angle to his time as \u2018Prince Emeritus\u2019 in Los Angeles: his replacement being exactly the sort of Kindred he\u2019d want to see in charge allows for a fascinating clash between the natural desire to reclaim his city and an awareness that he would have to actively sabotage not only his rival, but the city itself to get back where he would like to be\u2026<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T10:17:44-08:00","id":1548369,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, my presumption would be that the Palatine treaty allowed the San Francisco prince and primogen authority to negotiate with the Anarchs as and when necessary, with a minimum of oversight from the Inner Circle - in essence allowing a single city at least some freedom to set policy for the whole Camarilla when it came to the Free States Anarch movement (Absolutely necessary when San Fran was on the lion\u2019s lip, deals needed to be made Right Now on a nightly basis and the arrival of any Camarilla heavy hitters would be an excellent excuse for the beast to bite down, but also the sort of Liberty* that would make some on the Inner Circle nervous \u2026 or cross).<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*In the classic, \u2018Civic Privileges from Absolute Monarchy\u2019 meaning and not the \u2018Life \u2026 and Pursuit of Happiness\u2019 sense.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T21:43:54-08:00","id":1548419,"title":"","content":"One aspect not addressed so far is that if Tara is on the Anarch Council, her possible defection to the Camarilla is much more debilitating to the anarchs than simply losing San Diego. She would have inside knowledge of anarch operations in other domains. Losing San Diego would be bad. But Tara could bring down a lot of anarchs in a lot of Camarilla domains, crushing the opposition in wide swaths of North America.<br /> <br /> Tara seems to be an older style of anarch, the kind like Modius or even Maldavis which simply expected that overthrowing the Prince meant you got to become Prince and reward your own followers. She seems to resent that she can't simply rule San Diego because of MacNeil's and Salvador's ideals in the Status Prefectus. Tara would probably be more than happy to rule as an &quot;Anarch Prince&quot;, but that simply isn't possible while MacNeil is alive. Any attempt to rule like a Prince would be seen as a betrayal so her drift to the Camarilla would force her to be more aligned with the elders than otherwise.<br /> <br /> So one aspect in terms of player plot would be for the PCs to try to discover evidence of possible betrayal by Tara. MacNeil or possibly Salvador Garcia could act as quest givers. That would divert the game into more of a San Diego By Night than Los Angeles By Night, but it is an option. I'll discuss this more when I eventually post a thread on Justicar Petrodon's operations in the Free States. However, since Tara's role in the Anarch Council would be prominent, I think that is relevant here as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T22:05:19-08:00","id":1548420,"title":"","content":"I'm quite impressed with all the world building you put in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T04:22:15-08:00","id":1548427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548419#post1548419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One aspect not addressed so far is that if Tara is on the Anarch Council, her possible defection to the Camarilla is much more debilitating to the anarchs than simply losing San Diego. She would have inside knowledge of anarch operations in other domains. Losing San Diego would be bad. But Tara could bring down a lot of anarchs in a lot of Camarilla domains, crushing the opposition in wide swaths of North America.<br /> <br /> Tara seems to be an older style of anarch, the kind like Modius or even Maldavis which simply expected that overthrowing the Prince meant you got to become Prince and reward your own followers. She seems to resent that she can't simply rule San Diego because of MacNeil's and Salvador's ideals in the Status Prefectus. Tara would probably be more than happy to rule as an &quot;Anarch Prince&quot;, but that simply isn't possible while MacNeil is alive. Any attempt to rule like a Prince would be seen as a betrayal so her drift to the Camarilla would force her to be more aligned with the elders than otherwise.<br /> <br /> So one aspect in terms of player plot would be for the PCs to try to discover evidence of possible betrayal by Tara. MacNeil or possibly Salvador Garcia could act as quest givers. That would divert the game into more of a San Diego By Night than Los Angeles By Night, but it is an option. I'll discuss this more when I eventually post a thread on Justicar Petrodon's operations in the Free States. However, since Tara's role in the Anarch Council would be prominent, I think that is relevant here as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Curiously enough, I was trying to work out where to post some thoughts on Ms. Kearney (without disrupting this thread) before seeing these suggestions: one of my key sources for LA BY NIGHT is an online read-through and commentary on the book, and at least one of the reviewers expressed confusion regarding her actual character, as well as her motives for wishing to become a Camarilla Prince and not an Anarch Baron.<br /> <br /> At which point it immediately occurred to me that they key to understanding Tara Kearney\u2019s character is that she\u2019s the sort of woman who was sick of cowboy bull**** even when there were more cows than boys producing it: she settled the American Frontier once and by golly she refuses to live through the Wild West all over again (Not least because a key element in her motivation is that she wants to rebuild the family she lost and refuses to see it taken from her all over again).<br /> <br /> Given that Los Angeles, especially vampire Los Angeles, is absolutely full of Bull****, Cowboys and Cowboys Bull**** it\u2019s entirely unsurprising that she eventually gravitated towards the Camarilla (Which may be accused of many things, but never of tolerating Cowboy Bull**** if it can possibly bury it in an unmarked grave or bleach it to death instead).<br /> <br /> As the sort of pragmatic, motherly and commanding influence who did so much to settle the American Frontier (and impose some fairly stifling \u2018Civilised\u2019 values in the process) you could do worse than to make her the epitome of California\u2019s \u2018silent majority\u2019 elements. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying she has to be played by Ms. Kathy Bates (circa MISERY?), but that\u2019s who the character puts me in mind of.<br /> <br /> <br /> One other point about Ms. Kearney (I\u2019d bet that she much, much prefers to be addressed formally than as \u2018Tara\u2019, at least by persons whom she does not consider friends &amp; associates) which the read-through never really mentions is that she\u2019s noted to have put together a brood all her own - one that went it\u2019s own way during the War Between the States (Tara took too long to make her mind up, the brood got restless and therefore made up their own minds) but was brought back together by their progenitor\u2019s summons when she decided to move from Texas to California.<br /> <br /> All of which suggests that Tara\u2019s brood are going to be numerous, not lockstep-loyal to their sire, especially important in San Diego and probably far from uncommon (or without influence) in LA &amp; the Free States as a whole - heck, the \u2018family\u2019 might still have connections (or even an outpost) back in Texas.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also entirely possible that the \u2018Family Business\u2019 might split down the middle on Tara Kearney\u2019s defection to the Camarilla - with many following her to the Ivory Tower and others stubbornly going their own way (Tara may well have taken a seat on the Free States Council to expand her own interests and put less reliable members of her family somewhere she wouldn\u2019t have to kill them or be killed herself at the time<br /> of her defection*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>My impression is that she has a genuine aversion to All Out War, possibly a genuine dislike of violence as a whole (Bloodshed is one thing, but actual mayhem is another).</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T04:29:22-08:00","id":1548428,"title":"","content":"Also, whilst I really, really love the idea of Walter &amp; Millie Gaspars getting their grounding in Kindred society from the Vignes <i>m\u00e9nage</i> - very different generations of suburban respectability coming together for a comedy of manners with strong Gothic Horror elements sounds just right for these characters - it has also occurred to me that making the Gaspars descendants of Tara Kearney through one of the wilder spirits from her brood might be equally (or<br /> more) interesting.<br /> <br /> If only as a way to suggest that while Tara runs a tight ship, her judgement of persons isn\u2019t always flawless and she has a bad habit of letting her scions get away with murder \u2026 so long as they commit it away from home and mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T10:28:34-08:00","id":1548438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548420#post1548420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite impressed with all the world building you put in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always overprepare my chronicles because I'm actually not very good at winging things when PCs do something unexpected (which happens a lot). It is not that I don't have ideas, but I tend to freeze while I figure out if that actually makes sense. However, if I figure out how things work beforehand (at least in a general sense), then it is far easier for me to decide that things will happen this way or that way once the PCs do something. Other STs are much better than me on winging things out of the blue and still having it make sense.<br /> <br /> I also like having a sandbox style game in the sense that the PCs can do things other than just follow my plot hook for the night or a medium/long term plot. If the PCs suddenly decide to go here and screw around, it helps if I know what might already be there.<br /> <br /> The other advantage it gives me is that lots of little story seeds/plot ideas that I write down. Whenever things die down and players are looking for something else, I can go to my list and quickly pull the next hook for the next game session.<br /> <br /> I don't think Los Angeles By Night is a very good sourcebook, but when combined with other sourcebooks, there is a lot I can mine from it. I don't mind keeping names the same and building on certain ideas, but some characters and concepts are going to be different than how they are depicted in LABN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T11:15:56-08:00","id":1548442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548427#post1548427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiously enough, I was trying to work out where to post some thoughts on Ms. Kearney (without disrupting this thread) before seeing these suggestions: one of my key sources for LA BY NIGHT is an online read-through and commentary on the book, and at least one of the reviewers expressed confusion regarding her actual character, as well as her motives for wishing to become a Camarilla Prince and not an Anarch Baron.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am only going by what is written in the original Los Angeles By Night sourcebook as I dislike much of what was developed in Revised. Like most character descriptions in LABN, we're actually not given much information about the character. Most of it is just filler geared towards immediate needs. Unlike the stronger sourcebooks, we're given little motivation and detailed backstories for most characters and have to create our own details if we want them to be real characters.<br /> <br /> Tara isn't even given a last name in LABN. We know she was born in 1794 and embraced in 1822 so she's a product of early American independence. It makes sense that she'd be a product of the American frontier, but in her mortal days this probably meant Tennessee or similar, and she worked her way over to Texas by the 1940s.<br /> <br /> She's described as slightly overweight which is surprising for someone in her mid-twenties from that era. People worked hard back then and unlikely to have extra weight so young. So I imagine her as a more stocky, hardy frontier type. Probably with some weight gain from pregnancy, but hardly &quot;overweight&quot;. Unusually for LABN, she's only average-looking. The author really liked female characters who were extremely attractive in their mid-to-late teens. So I just interpret that to mean the author didn't want Tara to be hot because she's likely one of the antagonists, and he wouldn't want PCs to take her side because of her attractiveness.<br /> <br /> By the time of the 1944 revolt, Tara was supposed to be a &quot;well known anarch from Texas&quot; so she already had a reputation. She arrived with &quot;13 Brujah fighters, many of them veterans from the American Civil War.&quot; I'm sure part of that was some of her brood. I imagine Tara took part in the struggle against the Southern Lords and any Ventrue or Toreador Princes who ruled any of the southern cities.<br /> <br /> Tara lead the anarch attack on San Diego. LABN says she claimed the area as her own in &quot;the first land grab&quot; so she's actually the very first &quot;baron.&quot; The other anarchs on the Revolutionary Council (that ruled the Free States until the Status Prefectus abolished it in 1945 or so) were &quot;too busy&quot; to argue so she got away with it. So her desire to rule her own plot of land was very early.<br /> <br /> Strangely, it mentions Tara arrived with the Prince of San Diego (someone named Maria) already destroyed. We're not told by who. Local anarchs who destroyed the Prince, but were destroyed by the surviving elders? Lupines? Sabbat? Hunters? In any case, being right next door to the Sabbat in Mexico would be an incentive for someone to want to hold real power. Being a much smaller domain, San Diego anarchs don't have the luxury of the immense population of the LA metro area.<br /> <br /> One thing I am leaning to is the idea of having &quot;Tijuana Anarchs&quot; and Tijuana, Mexico being a battleground between Anarchs and Sabbat. Tijuana is part of the same metro area as San Diego. Actively fighting the Sabbat there would help protect San Diego proper. And it provides another incentive for Tara to cooperate with certain Camarilla officials. She needs help protecting her domain, and the anarchs in LA proper just aren't contributing enough. I can see someone becoming resentful because of that.<br /> <br /> Tremere Clanbook, Revised gives us Joseph Ravenfeather, a Tremere of Indian ancestry who studied Indian &quot;shamanism&quot; and may have been the only Tremere in San Diego prior to the revolt. He quickly worked with Tara and gained acceptance. The character description isn't very good or coherent once you start looking at its details, but it's a good enough to work with. So I'm going to use him as another Kindred in San Diego, and someone whom Tara can rely on against the Sabbat. He straddles the fence between anarch and Camarilla loyalist, but is a conduit to his &quot;superiors&quot; in the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T13:42:26-08:00","id":1548447,"title":"","content":"As a note, I tend to get the gist of various characters from that online \u2018Let\u2019s Read\u2019 of LA BY NIGHT mentioned earlier and biographical details from the WHITE WOLF WIKI articles - assuming the characters are lucky enough to get an article to themselves, which not all do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tara_Kearney\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tara_Kearney</a><br /> <br /> <br /> As it happens, Prince Tara Kearney does, so I was able to build my mental image of the character from there and the article includes some interesting details, like the fact that she was Prince of El Paso until the Civil War - apparently building a following from other neonates, though implicitly building up a brood of her own as well - that she declined to take sides between the North &amp; the South (Resulting in her brood scattering to follow their own opinion); that she moved to Dallas during the conflict but was unable to establish herself as Prince or in any other position of prominence there (Purportedly for being too junior, though one wonders if quitting her own city and lacking a coterie of her own might also have played a part in this - that the local Kindred kept her under scrutiny is potentially revealing); having been forced to abandon El Paso due as much to economic factors, she proceeded to familiarise herself with economics to make good her previous weaknesses in this area; that almost a century after her brood scattered she was able to call them together once again and move on San Diego with this following (Though it took a coup and her own counter-coup to consolidate this conquest).<br /> <br /> All of this seems to be cromulent: it\u2019s also interesting to note that her sire, one Justin Davies, was an 8th Generation Brujah active in Texas circa the 1820s. Given he shares the same generation and Clan as Jeremy MacNeil, one could semi-plausibly suggest a connection between two of the more prominent Brujah in the Free States (One that would lend an especially interesting dynamic to LA/San Diego relations).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Working from your own list of facts established in LA BY NIGHT, it seems reasonable to deduce that Tara was of Irish descent (Tara being the seat of Ireland\u2019s high king, as well as the place of their acclamation) - it\u2019s possible that the name was adopted at a later date, but the fact she chose it all suggests it has some significance for her.<br /> <br /> - I definitely agree with the notion of Tara as more \u2018human average\u2019 than \u2018overweight\u2019 (Given this was a description penned by somebody working from the \u2018liquid diet for a hundred plus years\u2019 standards of Vampire Romance), hence my mental image of the character as played by Ms. Kathy Bates.<br /> <br /> - It seems plausible to suggest that Tara may have targeted San Diego precisely because it lacked a Prince at that point in time (She strikes me as more than shrewd enough to present herself as more a peacemaker than a conqueror and to prefer a headless enemy): whether it lacked a Prince because the first stage of the Anarch Revolt had already done her in or perhaps because she suffered some Sabbat-Anarch related misfortune - persuading Don Sebastian of LA to grow steadily more tyrannical before the Second Anarch Revolt precisely because he\u2019d seen one Prince in the region pulled down already (Very possibly one of his own blood, given that probably-Hispanic name and the necessity of maintaining an outpost on the fringes of Sabbat Mexico to the Prince of LA) is a question for the individual storyteller to answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> - I do like the idea of Tijuana as THE Anarch outpost in Southern California before Los Angeles revolted and the Free States were established, as well as something of \u2018frontier warfare\u2019 zone thereafter: it makes sense that vampires in Southern California would want somewhere they didn\u2019t have to worry about being nailed down by Don Sebastian\u2019s boys and offering their services as hired guns against the Sabbat to Maria might have been just enough to earn them their little hole in the wall (Not to mention a useful safety valve, albeit too small to keep Los Angeles working smoothly in the long run, especially if Maria was the one who persuaded Don Sebastian to maintain that safety valve properly in the first place).<br /> <br /> Of course after the Second Anarch Rebellion the old three-sided duel of wits might well become more of a straightforward clash of wills between Anarch and Sabbat (Though it\u2019s quite possible that a local tradition of Anarch and Sabbat back-and-forth against the Camarilla might complicate the local dynamic, with the new local Prince tolerating Kindred she might otherwise oust precisely because she wants to maintain the local balance of power, at least in terms of armed force).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, the notion of Tara already being something of a known Anarch in Texas would definitely explain why she was kept a carefully eye on whilst in Dallas.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Finally, it\u2019s intriguing to speculate on the presumably-complex relationship between OG settler matriarch Tara Kearney and Joseph Ravenfeather of Clan Tremere: any situation that can be described as a \u2018land rush\u2019 is likely to give the latter some seriously unhappy flashbacks even as the former is likely to be completely in her element.<br /> <br /> <br /> Please pardon this somewhat messy summary of notions: I\u2019ll try to do better tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T14:07:23-08:00","id":1548449,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, I intended to comment earlier on your own article but am (As mentioned elsewhere) trying to brush up on LA BY NIGHT first: however, I did want to suggest that there are a number of interesting possibilities for the identity of the \u2018LA Ripper\u2019, for my money the most inherently interesting identify for their Sire would be a Ventrue.<br /> <br /> If nothing else this would suggest the most interesting possibly dynamic between the late Sire and Prince Sebastian La Croix (The Ventrue emphasis on Clan Loyalty would make the Sire\u2019s rebellion against the Prince all the more telling and a public display of the willingness to come down hard on one from his own Clan might help justify Prince La Croix\u2019s failure to dispose of an old rival and their inconvenient Childe more privately, whilst also making it clear that the Prince is handicapped by his own sincerity and love to public display).<br /> <br /> This also helps explain why there\u2019s no Primogen to protest the Childe\u2019s treatment by Prince La Croix and sets up the Prince &amp; the PC as mirror image foils to each other, which none of the other origins do (Heck, the chance to order around a spawn of his old rival like a good cabana boy or girl might help explain why the Prince spares an illegal creation in the first place, especially given the chance at a win-win scenario as he orders them into various probably-lethal missions).<br /> <br /> In fact it occurs to me that David Geduld (Chicago Ventrue sent into Los Angeles as a Camarilla agent gone native in the Anarch Free States) might be especially perfect in the role, since he becomes a much more interesting character in a Los Angeles at least notionally controlled by the Camarilla - presumably using his personal connections &amp; inside knowledge of how the system works to cover for old Anarchs and make life more difficult for the new Prince - only for his own ambition and passions to make him a martyr to his cause.<br /> <br /> That this would make the LA Ripper a female Ventrue also adds something interesting to the various interpersonal dynamics (and Geduld\u2019s personal connections to the Anarch movement would help explain why the Old Anarchs make a point of supporting this Childe).<br /> <br /> CTPhipps, I know your heart belongs to the Malkavians (As to all things Chaotic) but hopefully this is at least a potentially interesting counter-suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T09:23:57-08:00","id":1548495,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I hope my posting is not too repetitious and that it\u2019s been somewhat helpful - if only by inspiring you to come up with better ideas all your own - and I also wanted to further test your patience by advocating for the Nosferatu member of the Free States Council to be an affectionate pastiche of vampire characters from ANGEL: THE SERIES (Based, of course, on the crackpot theory that the most interesting way to work BUFFY vampires into the World of Darkness would be making them Nosferatu - since this would pay tribute to the makeup jobs in that series, whilst also highlighting the considerable differences between Kindred and some of the more famous vampires to terrorise/romance/sleuth/punk their way across Southern California).<br /> <br /> <br /> I suggest this because:-<br /> <br /> (A) BUFFY/ANGEL is one of the most famous depictions of vampires in any context<br /> <br /> (B) The specific context iof the show is, in fact, Southern California and Los Angeles proper<br /> <br /> (C) It therefore makes sense to include one or more homages to one or both of these shows <br /> <br /> (D) With this in mind, ANGEL makes more sense as a model than BUFFY, because sometimes, just sometimes, even Anarchs need lawyers (Also, guilt-ridden vampire hero in LA is much more MASQUERADE than one of the most famous heroic vampire hunters in fiction who is not actually a vampire).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019m doing this on my smartphone so this has to be more of a character sketch, but here\u2019s what I have so far:-<br /> <br /> <br /> - This character is of the Tenth Generation (As a \u2018Gen X\u2019 joke)<br /> <br /> - This character is of Clan Nosferatu, but hails from a branch of the bloodline that is \u2026 well to put it simply they\u2019re a Cult. Possibly a Noddist cult, definitely descending from and, to some extent, still answering to a leader who (from the perspective of the 1990s) has only recently been unburied after suffering a rather nasty accident during the 20th century (Possibly entering a fairly brief Torpor) and taken over a small town on the outskirts of Los Angeles that had a vampire problem to start with and is now suffering a potentially \u2018End of Human Civilisation in Southern California\u2019 problem<br /> <br /> <br /> Note: for the record, I\u2019m assuming that this nameless pastiche of Sunnydale-on-the-Hellmouth is experiencing a status quo comparable to that seen in \u2018The Wish\u2019 timeline (Where no superhero vampire slayer showed up, the day went unsaved and various well-beloved supporting characters went very, very Bad as a result, with the result that an elder vampire is currently working on a device that will rip the blood out of human prey faster than a juicer sucks an orange dry).<br /> <br /> Not least because this is a very WORLD OF DARKNESS status quo that would make an excellent starting point for an adventure where the slightly-less-evil vampires show up and take the problems of a small California town with some<br /> interesting secrets upon themselves, however briefly.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Anyway, regarding the character under construction, my mental image was of a character who combines elements from both Angel and Spike (Given that the former\u2019s Magical Curse doesn\u2019t really work in a VtM context and because, let\u2019s face it. The latter\u2019s \u201cLet me be Evil and Fun! Aargh, Evil hurts! Therefore I shall fight some Evil and get my kicks that way. Hey, that Hero is not only hit, she and her fellow heroes provoke both thought and feelings. Wait, Evil no longer hurts, but I still want to fight some Evil and do some Good? Right oh!\u201d character arc is, in many respects, far more compelling).<br /> <br /> Where was I? Oh yes - the character would be somebody embraced because a vampire wanted somebody fun to spend eternity with; adapted well enough to being a deformed creature of the night because, honestly, they were a passionate romantic and the idea of somebody wanting to spend all eternity with them really floated their boat; didn\u2019t get on very well with the aforesaid Cult Leader grandsire and was allowed (or encouraged) to go their own way (Possibly in the hopes that they would die alone); obstinately continued to live, fight and be ruled by their passions; eventually guilt-tripped their way into anti-heroism; experienced a really bad break up as a result; decided to get an actual job and settled on Vampire Private Eye; experienced a series of adventures that pitted them against (Amongst other things) an organisation of Evil SUPERNATURAL Lawyers and, possibly by giving said law court sharks a choice between \u2018Hostile takeover\u2019 and \u201cFirst we kill all the lawyers\u201d acquired a level of control over said Law Firm.<br /> <br /> - At this point I\u2019m not entirely clear on what their exact origin is: I\u2019m assuming they\u2019ve been a vampire since the 19th century , at the least; that the progenitor of their lineage was a vampire who arrived in California claiming to be acting at the behest of Don Armando de Madrid (Seeking one Alonzo Guillen, a Childe who went MIA during the Nineteenth century) and proceeded to spend much more time establishing their own power base in Los Angeles (Very possibly as the progenitor of the local Nosferatu lineages) before departing the city under ambiguous circumstances (Did he leave or was he pushed? The Hollywood Nosferatu aren\u2019t telling).<br /> <br /> - Whether the character in question followed after \u2018Grandsire\u2019 or was made in the Old World and then followed after I\u2019m not sure: one definitely imagines him playing some role in the Second Anarch Revolt (Probably as his way of getting out from under \u2018Abuello El Caudillo\u2019 with support from his new friends and associates, but increasingly for the sake of the Anarch cause).<br /> <br /> - At this point I tend to imagine his role on the Anarch Council as \u2018human whisperer\u2019 (Having built up a crew of loyal assistants, not least to act on his behalf in the daylight hours and as the \u2018face\u2019 whi deals with clients), not least in that he takes at the very least a professional interest in dealing with same - rather than tending to focus on Vampire politics as a world unto itself, a tendency not infrequently on display in the Free States Council.<br /> <br /> Given his association with a law firm, it seems highly likely he takes a particular interest in identifying and countering Camarilla efforts to extend their influence into the Free States by covert daylight channels, as well as seeking to cause legal problems for the Camarilla in nearby territories.<br /> <br /> Being a Nineties vampire detective he likes to keep his hand in by doing some of the legwork himself (He\u2019s not much inclined to katanas, but he LOVES the leather duster with a love surpassing the love of woman); he also still displays a dangerous tendency to help the helpless, for fun and profit and because he feels at least a little guilt for his years as a mean *******, which will obviously keep him in trouble.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I\u2019d bet money he has some interesting history with non-vampire supernaturals (It also seems likely he has a history of intense and increasingly-dysfunctional romances, if only with his fellow Nosferatu, but quite possibly with other beings \u2026 probably at a distance, given his Clan Curse). <br /> <br /> <br /> Might I please ask if there\u2019s enough in the character to be worth developing further? Any thoughts on how to make him fit more elegantly into the World of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T12:11:30-08:00","id":1548498,"title":"","content":"While I am obviously looking for feedback and good ideas I want to use, the thread also exists for people to develop their own ideas on the topic, and hopefully to inspire others in designing their own game in the Free State. So as long as it is on topic, go ahead and post.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I never watched Buffy or any spinoff show. I just was not interested. I did see the original Buffy movie (years before the TV show), but thought it mediocre and not to my tastes. I was surprised when it became a TV show I know the TV show is held in high regard and had many friends watch it, but it never had an appeal to me. My general opinion of Joss Whedon tends to be, &quot;Didn't I already read this in a Chris Claremont comic book?&quot;<br /> <br /> At some point, I will be contacting my players for initial character creation and preludes, and as part of that I will be asking them OOC things they want to see included in the chronicle from the perspective of vampire media in general and media taking place in LA. Examples I'll be using are flying vampires from the Lost Boys (some anarchs will know Movement of Mind) and Nakatomi Plaza from Die Hard. So it is entirely possibly one of them might mention Sunnydale or some other element of Buffy. If so, I might be reaching out for some guidance. Personally I'd rather have Detective Axel Foley be a vampire hunter than Buffy, but we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T13:36:09-08:00","id":1548568,"title":"","content":"Message received, though I think it\u2019s fair to warn you that even after revelations that Mr Whedon could be \u2026 <i>difficult</i> \u2026 quite a few fans of Vampire (or vampire adjacent) fiction will have their perception of South California vampires shaped by the Buffy-verse in some form or the other.<br /> <br /> Also, if you\u2019re looking for an oddball occult investigator working in So-Cal, you could do worse than BAYWATCH NIGHTS (You can do So Much Better, but at least David Hasselhoff - I mean Mitch Buchanan - has actual experience of dealing with things that go BUMP in the night).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T13:37:41-08:00","id":1548569,"title":"","content":"Any fans of BUFFY browsing these threads should be wanted that I would absolutely read a BAYWATCH/BUFFY crossover (and probably even share it with the community were one to find it): Reader, ye Be Warned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Olde-fashioned language be required. 02-18-2025, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T18:03:28-08:00","id":1548576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548568#post1548568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you\u2019re looking for an oddball occult investigator working in So-Cal, you could do worse than BAYWATCH NIGHTS (You can do So Much Better, but at least David Hasselhoff - I mean Mitch Buchanan - has actual experience of dealing with things that go BUMP in the night).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to figure out how to use this now. Maybe Mitch Buchanan discovering Karen Anotos, and the two somehow fulfill every single vampire movie cliche in a long running rivalry since Mitch never identifies any other vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XwVXiJeMYbg\" data-code=\"XwVXiJeMYbg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XwVXiJeMYbg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T13:41:48-08:00","id":1548597,"title":"","content":"Truly, BAYWATCH is the gift that keeps on giving when you\u2019re in search of good, wholesome 1990s cheese (Whether or not you\u2019re looking for cheesecake on the side).<br /> <br /> Heck, even the main series had at least one ghost and an actual mermaid!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T09:29:36-07:00","id":1549397,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019ve been meaning to as - how are your preparations for a Free States game proceeding?<br /> <br /> Have these various threads been at all helpful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T00:02:09-07:00","id":1549403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1549397#post1549397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have these various threads been at all helpful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. There are many suggestions and comments from these posts I'll be adding. There are definitely some characters who will be there as a result of other people's posts, twists or aspects, or connections between characters that I had not considered. Then there are some ideas that I may not be using, but which are strong enough that I'll be keeping them in my pocket if it turns out my players prefer something else than I what I initially do.<br /> <br /> Even when I just explain my ideas and don't get much comments on them, the process of having to think them through enough to write them down helps flesh them out. And simply not hearing certain ideas are terrible seem to be proof that they're solid enough to work. Even when people disagree, it's a good check for me on other people's tastes or pointing out weaknesses. It's also been good to hear what things other people like from the books and what they would do running the Free States. That's just as useful, or sometimes even more, than comments on my own ideas and interpretations.<br /> <br /> So thanks to everyone's who's contributed or even just hit the Like.<br /> <br /> There are definitely more posts and even new threads I'll be making, but I'm still organizing my thoughts on them and dealing with real life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T13:44:06-07:00","id":1549415,"title":"","content":"This is somewhat tangential to the core of the thread but with enough connections to make it worth including imo.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never really understood the rationale for having the New Anarch Revolts (here referring to the ones which produced the West Coast Free States rather than the First Anarch Revolt, the revolts that produced the \u2018Brujah Council\u2019 of the USSR, or the contemporary revolts of the early 1990s) take place in the 1940s rather than the seemingly natural pick of the 1960s. Maybe for Gen Xers in the 90s it being so natural was the problem, it was too obvious. But I mean, it would be natural for a reason.<br /> <br /> Southern California in the 1940s, to play Devil\u2019s advocate, does have some things going for it tbf. You\u2019ve got the waves of unrest produced by the Great Depression which certainly produced political ferment in real life (you had Upton Sinclair\u2019s EPIC program, but also groups like Ham and Eggs &amp; Technocracy Inc.). You had waves of Oakie immigrants who (of the Steinbeck tradition), alongside the early Chicano\u2019s, could possibly provide a base. You had the New Deal programs which finally ended LA\u2019s tenure as an anti-labor \u2018Open Town\u2019 and which gave the left room to breathe thanks to the Popular Front. You had Japanese internment which could have functioned as a \u2018barrack of revolt\u2019 hypothetically.<br /> <br /> Yet on the other hand this is still coming in the wake of the put-down of organized labor in Southern California post-WWI and in the 1920s. This is also post the Water Wars which helped to entrench the ruling powers and the rise of Hollywood Land. Furthermore imo the conditions of Southern California as a major military camp and manufacturing hub would dampen the potential for revolt - Military MPs everywhere, anti-saboteur vigilance, the anti-strike pledge from labor, and the generalized atmosphere of paranoia (see the Battle of Los Angeles) would imo strengthen the Camarilla during this period by making clear the absolute necessity of upholding the Masquerade. Hell that\u2019s part of what makes Hollywood so valuable - it was, alongside the news network hubs back east, a crucial wing of the state\u2019s propaganda arm. If the toreadors couldn\u2019t thrive in such an environment they wouldn\u2019t be worth their bulls.<br /> <br /> The humans would simply be too edgy to risk much going on outside the shadows. Besides that the war economy was a boon to organized crime, who were virtually given a blank check to manage the black market, so long as they kept saboteurs off the docks. In this atmosphere I can\u2019t help but see the Camarilla thriving; fattening themselves on internment profiteering, war profiteering, and black market profiteering.<br /> <br /> Then what about after the war ends? There was a bit of a post-war slump after V-Day, that\u2019s true, so maybe you put the revolt there. But I still don\u2019t really see it. The slump ends pretty quickly once the Korean War gears up. Besides that the post-war economic engine gets running pretty soon. The suburban sprawl in Southern California takes on new life in this period and the automobile nation proper is born. Plus the Military-Industrial Complex takes root and really makes cities like San Diego come to life, not to mention the sci-fi wonders coming out of places like Cal Tech. Then you get into the era of the Second Red Scare, from McCarthy &amp; HUAC to the anti-Beatnik hysteria to the teen delinquency-hysteria, all the way to Goldwater and the Orange County suburban warriors coming into self-consciousness.<br /> <br /> For me the Southern California of the 1930s through to the 1950s (including perhaps the 20s &amp; early 60s), especially LA, is the prime real estate for Noir. IMO that works best, in vampire terms, by having the Camarilla still running the show.<br /> <br /> I do think there would be a ferment however, the seeds of what would become the new Anarch Revolt. The old-old left in Southern California may have been beaten down after the era of the First Red Scare post-1917 and through the 20s, but there would be survivors, especially amongst the immortal. You had the Steinbeckian figures of the 1930s alongside the noir anti-heroes, the flakes of the nervous breakdown of the middle classes, the rising old left of the popular front and their liberal counterparts in the New Deal tangling with the rise of the Californian answer to brown shirts while exiled European intellectuals sought security in Hollywood. You had the rise of Noir proper with the 1940s and the question of the post-war order, amidst even further booms in population under the War economy (concentration that, even if they had accepted War-time Masquerade protections measures, would certainly have felt tensions building). You had the post-war answer in the Second Red Scare and HUAC which forced the comrades and fellow travelers back underground (those who didn\u2019t flee to Mexico City or Moscow at least). You also had the run-wild paranoia and hysteria of the era produce more moral panics to provide anarch inspiration: hipster anarchs from the anti-Beatnik hysteria (paging Nick Cave), hotrod Anarchs from the anti-youth delinquency hysteria, and perhaps most significantly anarchs drawn from the rising discontent of a black and latino population chafing under Anglo rule and channeled through the rising civil rights movement. <br /> <br /> If you combine all the potential anarchs created by the past 50 years with the booming of the population in the 1960s as the children of the war are finally grown up then I think you have a much bigger recipe for a New Anarch Revolt than you do in the 1940s. Combine that with the waves of migrants called in by 1967 with the inauguration of the Summer of Love, the international ripple effect from the Cultural Revolution in China in 1966, and the possible catalyst (or at least mask for the spark) which can be provided for LA by the Watts Uprising of 1965, then I think you\u2019ve got a strong case for post-dating the New Anarch Revolt forward two decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T17:51:37-07:00","id":1549426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1549415#post1549415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve never really understood the rationale for having the New Anarch Revolts (here referring to the ones which produced the West Coast Free States rather than the First Anarch Revolt, the revolts that produced the \u2018Brujah Council\u2019 of the USSR, or the contemporary revolts of the early 1990s) take place in the 1940s rather than the seemingly natural pick of the 1960s. Maybe for Gen Xers in the 90s it being so natural was the problem, it was too obvious. But I mean, it would be natural for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no obvious reason why to place the revolt and creation of the Free States in 1944 (at least that I can tell). If we placed it in Paris during the French Revolution, everyone would nod their heads and say, &quot;Of course.&quot; Maybe that there is no real world reason is the point. (Another idea is that wartime Los Angeles would have prevented the Camarilla from doing what it would normally do to defeat such a mass rebellion. The US government was not going to let anything happen in LA that could undermine the war effort. It could break the Masquerade.)<br /> <br /> What is interesting about the revolt is that it is essentially a fraud. Most of the legendary actions about it are revealed in LABN as propaganda and cover story. What happened the night of December 21, 1944 is the coincidence of three different events in canon.<br /> <br /> The first is the Lupine attack on the Temple of Set in Malibu that wiped out any Setites (except Dawn) and many elders. The second is the destruction of Don Sebastian and many elders at his ranch east of LA. Although what happened is not explicitly described, my interpretation is that Christopher Houghton - angry that Don Sebastian had severely beaten his latest crush, Jeremy MacNeil - punished Sebastian and the other elders by unleashing his Presence 8 power that caused all other vampires to frenzy. The third is that MacNeil and his compatriots - Salvador Garcia, Louis Fortier, and some others - planned to rise that night and avenge themselves upon the elders. However, instead of actually doing anything, every time they arrived at some place they discovered someone else had already beaten them to it. Of course after that night, MacNeil and the other anarchs did hunt down and destroy any remaining elders and most of the other Camarilla loyalists in the next few months, but the hard work had already been done. Without the Lupines and Houghton, it's possible that MacNeil and others would not have only failed, but possibly been destroyed.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if we're meant to ask if this was just coincidence, or if there is something else that explains why these three events just happened to occur that night. Was this something that Christopher Houghton planned, doing something behind the scenes to make sure the Lupines and MacNeil's friends also attacked that same night? That character's description does include &quot;you will go to any lengths to assist the object of your affections, although always in secret.&quot; The Free States exist because Houghton had a crush on MacNeil and wanted to give him what he wanted - a city not ruled by any Princes.<br /> <br /> I'm not particularly fond of Christopher Houghton as a character because that every city had some powerful methusaleh pulling the strings had become old hat and boring by that point. There really needed to be some other chronicle secret than &quot;a methusaleh did it.&quot; However, if you want to go by canon, his whims and actions are the primary reason why LA is the way it is.<br /> <br /> I'm going to ignore Houghton entirely when I run the chronicle, but whether or not he actually exists isn't something I've decided because it's not going to impact how the chronicle turns out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T18:25:33-07:00","id":1549429,"title":"","content":"I kinda like Houghton, I think in part because he reminds me of Armand from the vampire chronicles, and just his whole gimmick is funny. I also think that he\u2019s way too old though and that he\u2019d work just as well, better even, just as a \u2018normal\u2019 elder, maybe 400 or 500 years dead. <br /> <br /> I also think that he\u2019s a fun character to have exist in LA but I don\u2019t like him as a central tentpole character, unless maybe I wanted to stress the whole \u2018no, really, the Jyhad is JUST, ancient vampires following their whims and leaving everyone else to suck it up\u2019 idea. Even then I think you can do something better imo. <br /> <br /> I do think it would be funny and work well to have Houghton be a sort of meta joke character. Yeah there\u2019s this elder in LA and he\u2019s following his whims but he\u2019s not some secret mastermind like Helena &amp; Menele, most of the important stuff that happens in LA is not part of his plan or anything, his main involvement is accidentally causing things to happen around him, which other people, who may or not be aware of his existence at all, take advantage of. <br /> <br /> I think that\u2019s funny but that it would work best by either committing to that being the central joke or having there be a \u2018real\u2019 plot tentpole in LA which Houghton is either tangential to and/or completely unaware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T18:27:16-07:00","id":1549430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1549415#post1549415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is somewhat tangential to the core of the thread but with enough connections to make it worth including imo.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never really understood the rationale for having the New Anarch Revolts (here referring to the ones which produced the West Coast Free States rather than the First Anarch Revolt, the revolts that produced the \u2018Brujah Council\u2019 of the USSR, or the contemporary revolts of the early 1990s) take place in the 1940s rather than the seemingly natural pick of the 1960s. Maybe for Gen Xers in the 90s it being so natural was the problem, it was too obvious. But I mean, it would be natural for a reason.<br /> <br /> Southern California in the 1940s, to play Devil\u2019s advocate, does have some things going for it tbf. You\u2019ve got the waves of unrest produced by the Great Depression which certainly produced political ferment in real life (you had Upton Sinclair\u2019s EPIC program, but also groups like Ham and Eggs &amp; Technocracy Inc.). You had waves of Oakie immigrants who (of the Steinbeck tradition), alongside the early Chicano\u2019s, could possibly provide a base. You had the New Deal programs which finally ended LA\u2019s tenure as an anti-labor \u2018Open Town\u2019 and which gave the left room to breathe thanks to the Popular Front. You had Japanese internment which could have functioned as a \u2018barrack of revolt\u2019 hypothetically.<br /> <br /> Yet on the other hand this is still coming in the wake of the put-down of organized labor in Southern California post-WWI and in the 1920s. This is also post the Water Wars which helped to entrench the ruling powers and the rise of Hollywood Land. Furthermore imo the conditions of Southern California as a major military camp and manufacturing hub would dampen the potential for revolt - Military MPs everywhere, anti-saboteur vigilance, the anti-strike pledge from labor, and the generalized atmosphere of paranoia (see the Battle of Los Angeles) would imo strengthen the Camarilla during this period by making clear the absolute necessity of upholding the Masquerade. Hell that\u2019s part of what makes Hollywood so valuable - it was, alongside the news network hubs back east, a crucial wing of the state\u2019s propaganda arm. If the toreadors couldn\u2019t thrive in such an environment they wouldn\u2019t be worth their bulls.<br /> <br /> The humans would simply be too edgy to risk much going on outside the shadows. Besides that the war economy was a boon to organized crime, who were virtually given a blank check to manage the black market, so long as they kept saboteurs off the docks. In this atmosphere I can\u2019t help but see the Camarilla thriving; fattening themselves on internment profiteering, war profiteering, and black market profiteering.<br /> <br /> Then what about after the war ends? There was a bit of a post-war slump after V-Day, that\u2019s true, so maybe you put the revolt there. But I still don\u2019t really see it. The slump ends pretty quickly once the Korean War gears up. Besides that the post-war economic engine gets running pretty soon. The suburban sprawl in Southern California takes on new life in this period and the automobile nation proper is born. Plus the Military-Industrial Complex takes root and really makes cities like San Diego come to life, not to mention the sci-fi wonders coming out of places like Cal Tech. Then you get into the era of the Second Red Scare, from McCarthy &amp; HUAC to the anti-Beatnik hysteria to the teen delinquency-hysteria, all the way to Goldwater and the Orange County suburban warriors coming into self-consciousness.<br /> <br /> For me the Southern California of the 1930s through to the 1950s (including perhaps the 20s &amp; early 60s), especially LA, is the prime real estate for Noir. IMO that works best, in vampire terms, by having the Camarilla still running the show.<br /> <br /> I do think there would be a ferment however, the seeds of what would become the new Anarch Revolt. The old-old left in Southern California may have been beaten down after the era of the First Red Scare post-1917 and through the 20s, but there would be survivors, especially amongst the immortal. You had the Steinbeckian figures of the 1930s alongside the noir anti-heroes, the flakes of the nervous breakdown of the middle classes, the rising old left of the popular front and their liberal counterparts in the New Deal tangling with the rise of the Californian answer to brown shirts while exiled European intellectuals sought security in Hollywood. You had the rise of Noir proper with the 1940s and the question of the post-war order, amidst even further booms in population under the War economy (concentration that, even if they had accepted War-time Masquerade protections measures, would certainly have felt tensions building). You had the post-war answer in the Second Red Scare and HUAC which forced the comrades and fellow travelers back underground (those who didn\u2019t flee to Mexico City or Moscow at least). You also had the run-wild paranoia and hysteria of the era produce more moral panics to provide anarch inspiration: hipster anarchs from the anti-Beatnik hysteria (paging Nick Cave), hotrod Anarchs from the anti-youth delinquency hysteria, and perhaps most significantly anarchs drawn from the rising discontent of a black and latino population chafing under Anglo rule and channeled through the rising civil rights movement.<br /> <br /> If you combine all the potential anarchs created by the past 50 years with the booming of the population in the 1960s as the children of the war are finally grown up then I think you have a much bigger recipe for a New Anarch Revolt than you do in the 1940s. Combine that with the waves of migrants called in by 1967 with the inauguration of the Summer of Love, the international ripple effect from the Cultural Revolution in China in 1966, and the possible catalyst (or at least mask for the spark) which can be provided for LA by the Watts Uprising of 1965, then I think you\u2019ve got a strong case for post-dating the New Anarch Revolt forward two decades.</div> </div> </div> </div> Looked at from another direction, you could make a case for the Second Anarch Revolt being triggered in part because the LA Toreador are doing well out of WWII whilst almost nobody else is - this would certainly be in keeping with Don Sebastian\u2019s demonstrated tendencies (A mistrust of non-Spaniards, a pronounced tendency towards tyranny and a somewhat fickle competence - when he was good he was extremely capable, when he was bad he was appalling).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, it\u2019s worth considering that the Camarilla\u2019s influence in LA was weak enough for the Prince and his cronies to hazard the Masquerade to the point of chasing starlets stark naked through the streets of Hollywood.<br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s also interesting to wonder if the greater openness of the 1960s could be depicted as the fruition of efforts by elements within the Free States to create an environment in which their revolution could finally get out from under the human authorities as they had thrown off the old vampiric regime (I do tend to think that vampire history should sometimes mirror, sometimes prefigure and sometimes be dragged along in the wake of human social &amp; political developments - with the Second Anarch Revolt being a case where the Free State vampires were a bit ahead of the curve).<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, it\u2019s not as though Film Noir vampire-style is completely off the table in Los Angeles and the Free States, whether pre-Revolt or even afterwards (The Free States are a big place, after all - it\u2019s not impossible some areas were business as Humphrey Bogart even while others were preoccupied with Big Political Developments).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I for one would be sorry to lose Christopher Houghton, since the most powerful elder in the Free States (Or at least in Los Angeles) being a sort of Shakespearean Peter Pan explains so much about their unpredictability and violence, whilst also allowing PCs to mostly go about their business without having to worry what he\u2019s doing at the moment.<br /> <br /> Also, I suspect there\u2019s a good deal of potential pathos in the character, as a boy robbed of both his childhood and of his chance to grow into manhood (Due to having been Embraced at a horribly young age in more ways than one), who finally escaped the domination of his Sire at the cost of his dignity, then sought a place where he could finally make something of his own dreams come true.<br /> <br /> Even if they were Cruel Dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T18:29:35-07:00","id":1549431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1549429#post1549429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda like Houghton, I think in part because he reminds me of Armand from the vampire chronicles, and just his whole gimmick is funny. I also think that he\u2019s way too old though and that he\u2019d work just as well, better even, just as a \u2018normal\u2019 elder, maybe 400 or 500 years dead.<br /> <br /> I also think that he\u2019s a fun character to have exist in LA but I don\u2019t like him as a central tentpole character, unless maybe I wanted to stress the whole \u2018no, really, the Jyhad is JUST, ancient vampires following their whims and leaving everyone else to suck it up\u2019 idea. Even then I think you can do something better imo.<br /> <br /> I do think it would be funny and work well to have Houghton be a sort of meta joke character. Yeah there\u2019s this elder in LA and he\u2019s following his whims but he\u2019s not some secret mastermind like Helena &amp; Menele, most of the important stuff that happens in LA is not part of his plan or anything, his main involvement is accidentally causing things to happen around him, which other people, who may or not be aware of his existence at all, take advantage of.<br /> <br /> I think that\u2019s funny but that it would work best by either committing to that being the central joke or having there be a \u2018real\u2019 plot tentpole in LA which Houghton is either tangential to and/or completely unaware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, Houghton was sired in the Elizabethan period and is, in fact, in the four-to-five hundred range (It\u2019s just that his Sire was of a low generation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T20:51:00-07:00","id":1550185,"title":"","content":"This is not directly relevant to the Anarch Council, but thought it was the best place to go. It's something the Anarch Council might export as part of its ongoing support to the Anarch cause in other domains.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Cookbook has an extended section on &quot;Libertas&quot;. It is mentioned as a counterpart of Humanity. The idea is that just as Kindred have varying amounts of Humanity, they have varying amounts of Libertas. It's a kind of gnostic philosophy in that the more one &quot;frees&quot; themselves from control of other beings, the greater one's consciousness is. Things like Dominate, Presence, and the Blood Bond degrades one's Libertas or at least can be seen as evidence of it. Freeing oneself from control of others increases it. Mortals suffer from this too, but the act of embrace ends up &quot;freeing&quot; the mortal slightly because of their liberation from &quot;Libertas-draining institutions of mortal society.&quot; Gaining a new perspective as a vampire does that. Now vampires just need to increase that higher perspective.<br /> <br /> Eventually, the adherents of Libertas believe, this will have physical effects (just like Humanity does). Physical effects will be things like vampires overcoming their vulnerability to wood (meaning stakes through the heart), fire, and even sunlight because they'll be free from such external controls/limitations.<br /> <br /> It sounds batshit insane, but that's because we players know there is no such mechanic. (Although it does sound like some things that the Ordo Dracul might believe in Vampire: the Requiem.) However, in character, who is to say there is anything wrong with the idea other than it hasn't been proven or disproven yet.<br /> <br /> This entire section reminds me a whole of lot of Philip K. Dick's works that were heavily infused with a gnostic worldview of reality not being what we think it is, and that we're being manipulated by higher powers wanting to keep us ignorant. It builds on a lot of pseudo-gnostic philosophy built into the World of Darkness, and can also be seen in the Malkavian clan and eventually Mage.<br /> <br /> The philosophy behind this is not the sole philosophy of the Kindred of the Free States. Indeed, it seems to be a minority view, but it seems the writers of the Anarch Cookbook intended this to be an important element. <br /> <br /> We don't see this at all in the LABN sourcebook. Other than a brief mention in the Status Prefectus, it doesn't get addressed at all. In fact a lot of things mentioned in the Cookbook and other very early material concerning the Free States seem to get dumped by the time LABN came out. If Andrew Greenberg was no longer Developer at that time, I would attribute it to different tastes of the new Developer. But he was still the Developer at the time of LABN so I wonder if he simply had second thoughts on the direction of the Free States. Maybe there was fan feedback pushing back on it.<br /> <br /> So I'll be introducing this concept into the chronicle. It's novel enough idea, and I think it deserves some effort of spreading to anarchs elsewhere. It transforms mere politics into a spiritual crusade. Its actual true adherents are a relatively small group and spread between several coteries. But a a substantial minority will at least make reference to it, even if they really don't do anything about it.<br /> <br /> I'll just need to get some cliff notes on Philip K Dick, Colin Wilson, and William S Burroughs so I can condense this into some kind of coherent thought good enough to explain in an RPG and perhaps not sound completely nuts (only partially nuts). I'll probably base any exponents of the philosophy in very Burroughs-like beatnik tones.<br /> <br /> I already intend to have Dr Raoul King (the obvious Hunter S Thompson homage in the original Clanbook Gangrel) show up to the occasional Rant, so why not a Burroughs analogue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T11:56:43-07:00","id":1550194,"title":"","content":"This being The World of Darkness, believing in something hard enough might even make this approach work \u2026 if it doesn\u2019t get enough practitioners killed first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T18:26:28-07:00","id":1550816,"title":"","content":"The Anarch Council (not actually mentioned in LABN but in the Brujah Clanbook) seems to be the Comintern of the Anarch Movement. It doesn't rule the Free States, but supports the anarchs in other domains in their attempts to free themselves from the princes. As such, understanding their successes and failures can be important especially because a common question from PCs could be, &quot;What exactly are they doing?&quot;<br /> <br /> This could just be an honest question. The PCs might just want to confirm the Anarch Council is doing something. However, one of the worst things that can happen is when PCs think important NPCs are idiots or losers because they can't accomplish anything and need the PCs to do everything. This happens, of course, because the ST/GM simply wants to give players something exciting to do, but doesn't consider how their presentation might undermine the reputation of the NPCs.<br /> <br /> I also think its an important question as one reason many players lost interest in the anarchs is that they just seemed to be losers who got lucky once. Showing there is some kind of struggle with both setbacks and victories shows the anarchs are doing something, and makes them more attractive. My players in this chronicle won't want to feel they are losers for being anarchs, but that MacNeil and other anarchs are making a difference.<br /> <br /> &quot;Support&quot; in this case probably being smuggling weapons, sharing advice, helping anarchs make their own connections, and sending militant anarchs to places where they can help in any &quot;big push&quot; to overthrow the local prince. Any specific ideas on what else they do would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> So what has the Anarch Council be doing since 1945? Thankfully we do have some examples of anarch activities in other parts of the world, and we can easily hook these examples back to the Council. I'll explain in the following posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T18:33:50-07:00","id":1550817,"title":"","content":"First, let's look at some regrettable failures.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Cookbook describes how a conflict between the anarchs and the prince in Detroit escalated into a five faction war (Anarchs vs Prince vs Primogen vs Setites vs Sabbat) that saw the Sabbat takeover and massacre everyone else. We're not given other information, but I would set this at the same time as the 1967 Detroit Riots. That makes the best sense to me. It makes a good example of why the anarchs need to be careful in their attacks on the Camarilla and understand how other parties might take advantage of the work they put into it and get a lot of anarchs killed. If PCs push too hard or complain the council isn't doing enough, this is a good story to tell them as a cautionary tale. I'll probably have as a local NPC someone who is a lone survivor of the Detroit anarchs.<br /> <br /> We also have the infamous Night of Rage during the 1968 Democratic Convention in Chicago. Chicago is basically the capital of the Camarilla in North America. The largest city they control and home to several powerful and influential Kindred of multiple clans. Taking the city would have been a huge victory for the anarchs. Instead, it became a terrible defeat. &quot;Never before had the Anarchs experienced an assault of this massacre.&quot; Over a hundred vampires from all over the world disappeared in one night. The anarch leadership of many cities had been wiped out. &quot;Princes across the country were free to crack down with brutal vengeance. Anarchs everywhere were on the run: an age of repression had dawned.&quot; I imagine a lot of success stories that MacNeil and company had obtained over the past twenty years were wiped out. This can be a powerful lesson at being too obvious or too direct. If the elders and archons can concentrate their forces even large numbers of anarchs can be lost. Of all the defeats the anarchs suffered since 1945, this should be the most painful.<br /> <br /> Defeats are important because they are remembered and often used to fuel grievances, memorialize fallen comrades, or as part of a story that ends in eventual victory. Slogans like &quot;Remember Detroit&quot; or &quot;Never Forget '68!&quot; can provide a sense of history of the struggle important to LA anarchs even though those are far away places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T18:37:21-07:00","id":1550818,"title":"","content":"However, we can also point to some successes.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Cookbook mentions Perth as a domain that was recently liberated by the anarchs and that many of the Gangrel &quot;princes&quot; of small cities/towns are either anarchs or sympathetic to them. This is repeated in A World of Darkness 2e which adds that the prince who was overthrown was Lumley of Clan Tremere. I'm going to call this the Perth Free State. NPCs will announce its &quot;liberation&quot; at the first Rant the PCs go to, and make sure some Aussie anarch reps thank MacNeil and the Council for their support. I might have Germaine and some other well known Anarchs come back with them, fresh from helping liberate Perth. That way the PCs can see the movement succeeding and that MacNeil and the council are doing something.<br /> <br /> VtM Corebook 2e mentions that Sabbat recently lost Miami, and Anarch Cookbook reveals this was mostly due to the anarchs, and that the anarchs mostly fight Sabbat there and not the Camarilla. While there is a Camailla declared prince in the city, I am going to hold that the anarchs actually hold most of the city. Everyone &quot;knows&quot; the prince doesn't really rule, and that it's more important for the anarchs to fight the Sabbat there than the Camarilla. It's not exactly clear when the anarchs took control, but it intersects with the time of Daliah's embrace in 1982. I am going to say the anarchs made their move soon after the 1980 Mariel boatlift of Cuban refugees and managed to &quot;win&quot; just before Miami Vice TV show came on the air in September 1984. Miami at this time had the combination of prosperity and high crime that LA was also known for. A potential Miami Free State on the east coast would be a huge win for the anarchs, and I imagine a lot of help is being sent this way. Miami would seem to be a big draw for Smiling Jack as it is near his old Caribbean pirate grounds.<br /> <br /> A World of Darkness (both editions) mentions that the anarchs are strong in London, and that Manchster/Liverpool (one domain since the '70s) is ruled by a Brujah Prince. There was an attempted anarch uprising in Birmingham in the '70s that was ruthlessly crushed. Toreador-rule Edinburgh allows anarchs to reside openly, but it is assumed the Toreador there could crush them if they wanted. The Anarch Cookbook mentions Liverpool is a &quot;strong haven&quot; for the anarchs. They are probably protected (and cynically used) by the Brujah Prince. I imagine Robin Leelend is active there. Belfast is mentioned as a contested city between anarchs (Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavian) and Ventrue. Supporting their brethren in the British Isles is probably an important agenda for the Anarch Council even though there is no Free State there. If they are ever able to establish a full blown Free State in the British Isles, it'll open up opportunities for them elsewhere in Europe.<br /> <br /> Anarchs are mentioned in Paris, but don't seem much of a threat. Assuming these are local anarchs with little help from the Council. The greater potential in Britain probably appears as a better bet. There is an anarch insurgency in Scandinavia, but this is probably more to do with the Valkyries rising from torpor, and while they do not approve of the Camarilla, they really aren't anarchs. Anarchs are mentioned in Spain, but don't seem to be doing much. It is often mentioned in Europe that many Sabbat disguise themselves as anarchs. The main story in mainland Europe seems to be that the anarchs are present, but is a problem that is being controlled.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Cookbook mentions a recent upheaval in Panama and a three way struggle between anarchs, Camarilla, and Sabbat fighting it with their retainers. It is probably a reference to the the 1989/1990 US invasion that ousted General Noriega. Needless to say control over the territory around the Panama Canal would have a lot of positive impact especially in terms of support from LA to the US east coast and Europe.<br /> <br /> There isn't much talk of anarchs elsewhere. That doesn't mean there are not young vampires who are classified as anarchs. Just that they are probably weak and powerless.<br /> <br /> Still, this gives us a good outline of the Anarch Council's strategy. Continue to disrupt the West Coast. Establish a foothold in Australia that might one day liberate that continent. Support the establishment of an east coast Free State around Miami. Help the anarchs in the British Isle. Try to control Panama so they can better support the anarchs around the Atlantic. PCs who want to hear that the anarch leaders are doing something will be gratified to learn that they are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T12:29:47-07:00","id":1550850,"title":"","content":"Given your description of Anarch movements in the British Isles being supported from the California Free States, I wonder if Petrodon moved against Stanford Warwick and the other legs of the New England Triad because he strongly suspected that they were if not supporting, then failing to interdict Anarchs heading for Great Britain?<br /> <br /> (It has also occurred to me that this operation might have been a movie on his part to assimilate/co-opt Stanford\u2019s network after the Justicar\u2019s own was very badly compromised by the capture and conversion of his eldest Childe by the Sabbat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T21:03:58-07:00","id":1550932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1550850#post1550850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given your description of Anarch movements in the British Isles being supported from the California Free States, I wonder if Petrodon moved against Stanford Warwick and the other legs of the New England Triad because he strongly suspected that they were if not supporting, then failing to interdict Anarchs heading for Great Britain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any support the Free States could provide to the British anarchs would obviously not be going through New England.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1550850#post1550850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It has also occurred to me that this operation might have been a movie on his part to assimilate/co-opt Stanford\u2019s network after the Justicar\u2019s own was very badly compromised by the capture and conversion of his eldest Childe by the Sabbat).</div> </div> </div> </div>Warwick's Web is simply part of Trajan's Web, and presumably much of Trajan's information network IS the Nosferatu information network. There are plenty of Nosferatu who are not part of it, or perhaps may not realize they actually are part of it. However, it is definitely one reason the Nosferatu know so much. Regardless of Petrodon's position in the greater Camarilla, I don't see a Nosferatu Justicar mucking with it. He probably already benefits from it and likewise provides it with some information he picks up. It's just how the Nosferatu operate.<br /> <br /> If there is some kind of local Web ran by some Seattle Webmaster that covers the Pacific Coast of North America, then I could see Petrodon attempting to have it serve his purposes as there is direct relevance. That might cause some acrimony among the local Nosferatu clan, but it could probably be straightened out as Petrodon attempts to balance his roles as a Justicar and an elder Nosferatu. If I decide to go down that route, I'll develop in the Petrodon/Camarilla thread though, not here.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T09:51:30-07:00","id":1550960,"title":"","content":"It does seem highly likely that Petrodon would be old and cautious enough to maintain a network specifically tailored to suit his needs and stocked with more than a fair share of his loyalists - Nosferatu clan loyalty is a powerful thing, but a Justicar probably has to worry about rivals within the Clan and about loyalty to the Camarilla as a whole, not just a part of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T16:48:55-07:00","id":1552706,"title":"","content":"Plans for the actual chronicle are near culmination for me. Final character creation and preludes are coming soon. So I am focusing more on actual chronicle plot needs and such than laying out the sandbox. One player has stated he wants to be involved in the Movement itself which is not surprising since the focus is on the Anarch Free States. However, there is a huge difference between a PC dwelling and doing things in the Anarch Free States and a PC being involved in the Anarch Movement. The Movement has already succeeded in LA so there is little to do there. The Movement is mainly concerned with helping anarchs in other cities - places where the characters are not at. I'm not running a chronicle in some other city, but in LA.<br /> <br /> So I need to figure out opportunities for this character while keeping the game in LA. Since the Anarch Council is the organ that supports the Movement, I am putting it here on this thread.<br /> <br /> I already have some ideas in mind. <br /> <br /> I'm obviously going to ask the PC how he thinks he can contribute. He'll have to sell himself to the important anarchs on the Council. Hopefully he can come up with some ideas of him being in LA and still being useful. There's always the possibility the PC can make use of certain Backgrounds or Disciplines or backstory that can be done &quot;out of area&quot;. I'll have to see if that comes to anything.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Council aren't going to utilize just anyone. They'll want people who show they are competent and loyal. So the PC will need to spend some time showcasing they are and providing bonafides. Eventually he'll succeed. While I will be putting most of this burden onto the PC, I will probably need to provide some OOC advice. So if you have any suggestions, I'd love to hear them.<br /> <br /> I'm also going to utilize the Vampire Club in San Francisco extensively. It's one reason why it exists and I created its own thread. It won't be hard for the PC to visit and the other PCs can easily piggyback on the visit so the entire player coterie is together. It's an ideal spot for meeting other characters, making deals, and collecting information. It won't put PCs into a dangerous spot as if they visited other domains more hostile to anarchs. Whether by planes, trains, or automobiles, they can leave LA, arrive there, and make it back over a weekend (or perhaps even one night). I have some intrigue already in mind, but if anyone wants to add any &quot;one game session plots&quot; I'd love to hear them.<br /> <br /> There are also things to do in LA itself with the &quot;maintenance&quot; of the domain. Spies, interlopers, raiders/saboteurs from the Camarilla, Sabbat, or even Independent Clans are a present threat. This is complicated because the Free States are not about having enforcement. You can't hook up with the Sheriff, Harpies, or Scourge because there are not any, and any attempt to do their tasks openly would not be acceptable to the anarchs. However, there is always opportunities for low key, subtle, and unofficial actions. Whether the player realizes the hypocrisy in that, I don't know. Again, if people have ideas, particularly of the &quot;one game session plots&quot;, I'm listening.<br /> <br /> There can also be things that are less obtrusive or less like enforcing the Six Traditions. New anarchs show up all the time in LA, often with zero knowledge about the city. In the setting itself, there is something like a welcome wagon at A Taste of LA. This is fairly bare bones though, and possibly the PC could do better. The PCs will be starting the chronicle as outsiders just arriving and going through the issues of orienting themselves, so they'll have some fresh perspective on the needs of such new Kindred.<br /> <br /> So what are your ideas? What do you think are some ways Kindred in LA can help out the Movement while still staying in LA (or at least the nearby area)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}